aises the right han\n   Idle_ShakeOff |  | ['idle emote gesture loop', 'standing, shakes the head no', 'QUATERNIU\n   Idle_Shield |  | ['shield idle stance loop', 'guarding: the left forearm held across th\n   Idle_Shield_Break |  | ['shield hurt once', 'the guard breaks: knocked back off balance with \n   Idle_Sword |  | ['sword idle loop', 'standing ready with a sword in the right hand', '\n   Idle_Talking |  | ['idle talk loop', 'standing and talking with hand gestures', 'QUATERN\n   Idle_TalkingPhone |  | ['idle talk prop loop', 'on the phone: right hand at the ear, left arm\n   Idle_Torch |  | ['idle prop loop', 'standing with one arm raised, holding up a torch o\n   Interact |  | ['interact once', 'reaches forward at chest height and works something\n   Jog |  | ['run loop', 'jog, in place', 'QUATERNIUS/Jog_Fwd_Loop']\n   LayToIdle |  | ['getup once', 'gets up from lying on the back to standing', 'QUATERNI\n   NinjaJump_Idle |  | ['jump air loop', 'airborne ninja pose held: body forward, arms swept \n   Pistol_Idle |  | ['gun idle loop', 'standing ready, pistol held low in both hands', 'QU\n   Punch_Cross |  | ['unarmed attack once', 'rear-hand straight punch with a hip turn', 'Q\n   Punch_Jab |  | ['unarmed attack once', 'quick lead-hand jab from the stance', 'QUATER\n   Push |  | ['interact push loop', 'leans in and shoves something heavy, stepping'\n   Sitting_Enter |  | ['sit once', 'sits down onto a seat (no chair is drawn)', 'QUATERNIUS/\n   Sitting_Exit |  | ['sit once', 'stands up from a seat', 'QUATERNIUS/Sitting_Exit']\n   Sitting_Idle |  | ['sit idle loop', 'seated at rest', 'QUATERNIUS/Sitting_Idle_Loop']\n   Sitting_Talking |  | ['sit talk loop', 'seated, talking with hand gestures', 'QUATERNIUS/Si\n   Spell_Simple_Idle |  | ['magic idle loop', 'holds a spell ready', 'QUATERNIUS/Spell_Simple_Id\n   Swim_Idle |  | ['swim idle loop', 'treading water, upright', 'QUATERNIUS/Swim_Idle_Lo\n   Walk_Carry |  | ['walk carry loop', 'walking with a box held in both arms in front, in\n   Zombie_Idle |  | ['zombie idle loop', 'hunched and swaying, arms hanging: a zombie at r\n   Zombie_Scratch |  | ['zombie attack once', 'lunges and claws down with both hands, then se\n   Bow |  | ['bow aim once', 'raises a bow from low to aim at head height, holds t\n   Bow Pull Back |  | ['bow attack once', 'raises a bow, nocks and draws the string back to \n   Bow Pull Hold |  | ['bow aim pose loop', 'holds a bow at full draw, aiming']\n   Bow Release |  | ['bow attack once', 'looses the arrow: the drawing hand springs back, \n   Dance Body Roll |  | ['emote dance once', 'a long dance: body rolls, arm waves and a dip, 6\n   Dance Charleston |  | ['emote dance loop', 'the Charleston: the knees swing in and out, the \n   Dance Reach Hip |  | ['emote dance once', 'a dance: hip pops, then one arm reaching high an\n   Dizzy |  | ['hurt idle loop', 'sways in place, unsteady, the head lolling']\n   Dodge_left |  | ['dodge once', 'throws the body to the left in a low lunge and recover\n   Dodge_left_RM |  | ['dodge root-motion once', 'throws the body to the left in a low lunge\n   Dodge_right |  | ['dodge once', 'throws the body to the right in a low lunge and recove\n   Dodge_right_RM |  | ['dodge root-motion once', 'throws the body to the right in a low lung\n   Fighting Idle |  | ['unarmed stance idle loop', \"a boxer's stance: fists up, bouncing lig\n   Fighting Right Jab |  | ['unarmed attack once', 'from the fighting stance, a straight right pu\n   Flying Forward Super |  | ['fly air loop', 'flying forward like a superhero, both arms stretched\n   Greeting |  | ['emote gesture talk once', 'lays the right hand on the chest and bows\n   Idle Hurt |  | ['idle hurt loop', 'stands hunched, holding the side, hurt']\n   Idle Listening |  | ['idle talk loop', 'weight on one leg, a hand on the hip, head cocked:\n   Idle_Subtle |  | ['idle loop', 'standing still, breathing gently']\n   Jumping Jacks |  | ['emote exercise loop', 'jumping jacks: the arms and legs scissor out \n   Ladder_Idle |  | ['climb idle loop', 'holds on to a ladder, hands and feet on the rungs\n   Ledge Hang |  | ['climb idle loop', 'hangs from a ledge by both hands, legs dangling']\n   Levitate Idle |  | ['magic air idle loop', 'floats in the air, knees drawn up, bobbing ge\n   Meditate |  | ['sit rest idle loop', 'sits cross-legged, hands on the knees, breathi\n   Pushup |  | ['emote exercise loop', 'push-ups: the body held straight, arms bendin\n   Shivering |  | ['idle emote loop', 'hunched with the arms hugged in, shivering with c\n   Sleeping |  | ['rest lie idle loop', 'lies on the back asleep, the chest rising and \n   Throw Object |  | ['throw attack once', 'winds up and hurls an object, dropping into a d\n   Victory |  | ['emote cheer once', 'jumps up with a fist raised in triumph and lands\n   Victory Fist Pump |  | ['emote cheer gesture once', 'pumps a fist down at the side in triumph\n   Zombie_Idle_Crouch |  | ['zombie idle crouch loop', 'crouched low and swaying: a zombie at res\n   Zombie_Rise |  | ['zombie getup once', 'rises from the ground: lying, sits up stiffly a\n   Cheer_One_arm |  | ['emote cheer once', 'cheers with one fist raised high']\n   Cheering_Two_Hands |  | ['emote cheer once', 'cheers with both arms raised overhead, waving']\n   Golf_idle |  | ['sport prop idle loop', 'stands over a golf ball, the club held low, \n   Help_One_Arm |  | ['emote gesture once', 'waves one arm overhead for attention: help']\n   Help_Two_Arms |  | ['emote gesture once', 'waves both arms overhead for attention']\ncmu.json 62 ['name', 'CMU']\n   $pick |  | \n   Walk_Loop |  | ['walk loop', 'An everyday walk at a steady pace, arms swinging loosel\n   Zombie_Walk_Loop |  | ['walk zombie loop', \"A zombie's shamble: head and shoulders slumped f\n   Jumping_Jacks_Loop |  | ['exercise loop', 'Jumping jacks: hop the feet apart while the arms sw\n   Boxing_Guard_Loop |  | ['stance unarmed loop', \"A boxer's guard: fists up by the face, bounci\n   Boxing_Jab |  | ['attack unarmed once', 'From the guard, a straight jab with the lead \n   Sword_Lunge |  | ['attack sword once', 'Swordplay: from a guard, a lunge forward with t\n   Run_Loop |  | ['run loop', 'A steady run, arms pumping. One stride cycle, in place']\n   Sneak_Loop |  | ['walk crouch loop', 'Sneaking: crouched low, stepping carefully, arms\n   Wounded_Walk_Loop |  | ['walk hurt loop', 'Limping on a wounded leg: a short careful step on \n   Hurt_Stomach_Walk_Loop |  | ['walk hurt loop', 'Walking hunched over, a hand clutching the stomach\n   Walk_Backwards_Loop |  | ['walk loop', 'Walking backwards at an easy pace. One cycle, in place'\n   Crouch_Walk_Loop |  | ['walk crouch loop', 'Walking crouched low on deeply bent knees. One c\n   Hop_One_Foot_Loop |  | ['jump loop', 'Hopping on the left foot, the right held up, arms out f\n   Punch_Combo |  | ['attack unarmed once', \"A fighter's punch combination from a guard: j\n   Stepping_Punch |  | ['attack unarmed walk once', 'Karate stepping punches (oi-zuki): a lon\n   Get_Up_Face_Down |  | ['getup once', 'Getting up from lying face down: push up on the arms, \n   Get_Up_From_Back |  | ['getup once', 'Getting up from lying on the back: sit up, roll to a k\n   Pick_Up_Box |  | ['carry item once', 'Walking up to a box, bending to lift it, and carr\n   Carry_Heavy_Box |  | ['carry once', 'Moving a heavy box: squat, lift with effort, carry a f\n   Sit_Down_Get_Up |  | ['sit once', 'Sitting down on a chair and getting up again (no chair i\n   Wave_Hello |  | ['gesture once', 'Waving hello with a raised hand']\n   Stretch_Yawn |  | ['idle rest once', 'A big stretch with a yawn, arms reaching up overhe\n   Curtsey |  | ['emote once', 'A curtsey: one foot behind, knees dipping, a small bow\n   Waiting_Loop |  | ['idle loop', 'Waiting impatiently: shifting weight from foot to foot,\n   Looking_Around |  | ['idle once', 'Standing a little hunched, looking warily about']\n   Gorilla_Walk_Loop |  | ['walk monster loop', 'A gorilla: hunched, knuckles low, a rolling hea\n   Frankenstein_Walk_Loop |  | ['walk monster zombie loop', \"Frankenstein's monster: stiff legs, arms\n   Chicken |  | ['monster once', 'A chicken, acted by a person: elbows as flapping win\n   Breakdance_Helicopter |  | ['dance once', 'Breakdance: on the floor, the legs sweeping round unde","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c21bae92-846f-4b71-8d0d-098b4791d47c","uuid":"eb2c3a47-c0d7-44f3-a684-e1e6a986f38a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:23:15.483Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Importing ready-made animation\n\nmy-3D2dge animates with code, but its rigs can also play animation made for 3D games. Imported animation is stored in one format that both people and AI models can read and edit: **readable key poses**, plain JSON with whole numbers (below). It is organised in **sets**:\n\n- **QUATERNIUS** (`src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js`): every free clip of [Quaternius' Universal Animation Library 1](https://quaternius.com/packs/universalanimationlibrary.html) and [Library 2](https://quaternius.com/packs/universalanimationlibrary2.html) (both CC0). 88 clips: 45 from the first library plus its T-pose, and 42 from the second. It is the library a game or a model picks from.\n- **MESH2MOTION** (`src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js`): the human animations of [Mesh2Motion](https://github.com/Mesh2Motion/mesh2motion-app) (CC0), from three origins:\n  - 86 of Quaternius' clips as Mesh2Motion re-exported them (one defective copy is skipped);\n  - 75 clips its contributors animated (ladder, wall and pipe climbs, ledge hang, bow, backflip, dodges, crawling, flying, dances, emotes, deaths);\n  - 16 it motion-captured itself with a Sony mocopi suit (fishing, golf, cheers, salutes, turns).\n\n  That makes 177 clips, and every one records which origin it came from (see [Where each clip came from](#where-each-clip-came-from)).\n- **CMU** (`src/mocap/sets/cmu.js`): 60 moments cut from the [CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database](http://mocap.cs.cmu.edu/) (2,548 takes, free for all uses), picked for what a game like Emberdeep needs: gaits (run, sneak, limp, clutching the stomach, crouched, backwards, a one-foot hop, each one cycle looping in place), traversal (a skid stop, a jump over, a dive roll, ducking under), fighting (a punch combination, blocks, karate front, roundhouse and side kicks, stepping punches, a jab, a sword lunge, a spinning jump kick), falls and three ways of getting up, townsfolk at work (sweeping\n- **HERO** (`src/mocap/sets/hero.js`): the 15 clips Emberdeep's hero, the Wanderer, has adopted (see [The hero's clips](#the-heros-clips-in-emberdeep)): 8 from QUATERNIUS and 7 from MESH2MOTION, picked with `tools/anim-set.mjs`. It is the only set the game ships.\n\n`examples/mocap-lab.html` plays any of the sets (**G** switches) on two figures:\n\n- **a look-alike of the libraries' mannequin**: an orange figure with an egg-shaped head and purple joint rings. Its proportions and limb thickness are measured from the first library's own mesh.\n- **the engine's hero** (the Emberdeep swordsman, an HD `Humanoid`), playing the same clip retargeted to his chibi build. His cape and hair follow, and in sword clips his blade follows his fist.\n\nBoth work in every view, at any camera turn or zoom, in slow motion and frame by frame.\n\nTo bring in another library, follow [Adding a library, step by step](#adding-a-library-step-by-step); [Where to get more animation](#where-to-get-more-animation) lists the sources, what they cost and what each one takes.\n\n## Pipeline\n\n```\n.blend / .fbx / .bvh ──tools/to-glb.py──▶ .glb\nCMU takes (.asf + .amc) ──tools/cmu.mjs get──▶ .cache/cmu ──tools/anim-import.mjs --cmu──▶ src/mocap/sets/cmu.js\nlibraries (.glb) ──tools/anim-import.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js ──tools/anim-set.mjs──▶ src/mocap/sets/hero.js\n                                                     │                                                    │\n                                                     └──────────── Mocap.load(set) ◀──────────────────────┘\n                                                                        │\n                                              lib.sample(clip, t) ──▶ Mannequin.draw / Mocap.drive(humanoid)\n```\n\n1. **Import** (Node, no dependencies):\n\n   ```\n   node tools/anim-import.mjs UAL1.glb UAL2.glb --sources UAL1,UAL2 --name QUATERNIUS \\\n     --catalog src/mocap/catalogs/quaternius.json --out src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js\n   ```\n\n   (`npm run mocap:import -- ...`; `--list` prints a file's clips and bones and writes nothing; `--clips A,B` imports only those; `--tol 30` is the key-pose budget in mm.) For each library it:\n   - recognises the rig: Rigify `DEF-` bones (Library 1) or Unreal-style names (`pelvis`, `spine_01`, `upperarm_l`; Library 2);\n   - measures the rest body from the T-pose, finds forward and right (heels to toes, left thigh to right), and fits how that library's animators share a turn of the hips-to-chest between the spine bones (Library 1: 0, 0, 0.25, 1; Library 2: 0, 0, 0.55, 1);\n   - samples every clip at 30 fps, runs forward kinematics to 36 body points, turns each frame into a readable pose, and keeps only the key poses needed to stay within the budget (`fit`);\n   - takes each clip's tags and description from the catalog, written by hand from watching each clip.\n\n   A clip whose name is already in the set (from an earlier library) is skipped, and a clip with no catalog entry is reported.\n2. **Pick a set for a game**: `node tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js --clips Death01,LayToIdle --name HERO --out src/mocap/sets/hero.js --credit \"...\"` (`npm run mocap:set -- ...`) copies those clips, key for key, with the proportions of the libraries they came from.\n3. **The set file** is one script that sets `window.MOCAP[name]` and needs no network. Its header comment carries the credit and the legend, so a model that opens the file can read it at once:\n\n   ```\n   (window.MOCAP = window.MOCAP || {})[\"HERO\"] = {\n   \"set\": \"HERO\", \"format\": 1, \"credit\": \"...\", \"from\": \"QUATERNIUS\", \"fps\": 30,\n   \"sources\": { \"UAL1\": { \"file\": ..., \"rig\": \"rigify\", \"rest\": {...} }, \"UAL2\": {...} },   // the bodies the clips were measured on\n   \"body\": { \"height\": 1829, \"segs\": [...], \"bands\": [...] },                              // the mannequin's measured mesh\n   \"fit\": { \"Death01\": [10, 71], ... },                                                    // average and worst error vs the capture, mm\n   \"clips\": { \"Death01\": { \"clip\": \"Death01\", \"src\": \"UAL1\", \"dur\": 2.4, \"loop\": false, \"tags\": [\"death\"],\n                           \"desc\": \"staggers and falls flat on the back\", \"keys\": [ ...key poses... ] }, ... } };\n   ```\n\n   | Set | Clips | Key poses | Size | Gzipped | As tokens |\n   |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   | QUATERNIUS | 88 | 1,295 | 378 KB | 72 KB | ~190k for all; a typical clip ~2,100 |\n   | MESH2MOTION | 177 | 2,798 | 800 KB | 155 KB | ~400k for all |\n   | CMU | 60 | 2,376 | 705 KB | 162 KB | ~360k for all |\n   | HERO | 15 | 238 | 74 KB | 17 KB | ~34k |\n\n   For comparison, the old raw form (every frame of the first library's 46 clips as base64 Int16) was 591 KB, 232 KB gzipped, and unreadable.\n4. **Play**: `const lib = Mocap.load(window.MOCAP.HERO)`. Then:\n   - `lib.clip(name)` returns the clip;\n   - `lib.sample(clip, t)` returns the pose at time t, in-betweening the key poses (loops wrap, one-shots hold their last pose);\n   - `lib.moveAt(clip, t)` returns how far a travelling clip has carried the body;\n   - `lib.blend(a, b, k)` crossfades two poses;\n   - `lib.text(clip)` gives the clip as a model reads it;\n   - `lib.replace(name, edited)`, `lib.restore(name)` and `lib.edited(name)` swap in an edited clip and back.\n\n   `src/mocap/readable.js` (`MocapReadable`) holds the format itself, shared by the browser and the Node tools.\n5. **Draw or drive**:\n   - `new Mocap.Mannequin(lib, { height }).draw(g, ox, oy, view, pose, facing)` draws the look-alike. It is built from shaded capsules sorted by camera depth, the way the engine's HD rigs are drawn.\n   - `Mocap.drive(humanoid, lib)` makes a `Humanoid` take `rig.mocap = pose` after it poses itself.\n\n## Adding a library, step by step\n\nThis is the whole process of translating a 3D animation library into our format. Each step names its tool. Everything runs in Node, except the conversion from Blender, FBX or BVH files.\n\n**1. Check the license.** The converted set is committed to this public repository and ships inside games, so the source must allow sharing derived data.\n- CC0 is ideal.\n- CC BY works, with the credit in the set (`--credit`) and the README.\n....\nquaternius.json 89 ['name', 'UAL1', 'UAL2']\n   Idle_Loop |  | ['idle', 'standing at rest, breathing and shifting weight']\n   Idle_Talking_Loop |  | ['idle talk', 'standing and talking with hand gestures']\n   Idle_Torch_Loop |  | ['idle prop', 'standing with one arm raised, holding up a torch or lan\n   Jog_Fwd_Loop |  | ['run', 'jog, in place']\n   Crouch_Idle_Loop |  | ['crouch idle stealth', 'crouched low and still, looking about']\n   Punch_Enter |  | ['unarmed stance', 'brings the fists up into a fighting stance']\n   Punch_Jab |  | ['unarmed attack', 'quick lead-hand jab from the stance']\n   Punch_Cross |  | ['unarmed attack', 'rear-hand straight punch with a hip turn']\n   Sword_Idle |  | ['sword idle', 'standing ready with a sword in the right hand']\n   Spell_Simple_Idle_Loop |  | ['magic idle', 'holds a spell ready']\n   Pistol_Idle_Loop |  | ['gun idle', 'standing ready, pistol held low in both hands']\n   Interact |  | ['interact', 'reaches forward at chest height and works something with\n   Push_Loop |  | ['interact push', 'leans in and shoves something heavy, stepping']\n   Sitting_Enter |  | ['sit', 'sits down onto a seat (no chair is drawn)']\n  