{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GRz4p9356MUrr7ZjDXPAex","type":"tool_result","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module RHYTHM v0.88.0: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine only. Needs: no other module.\n\nPaRappa's, Beatmania's, Dance Dance Revolution's and Space Channel 5's play: notes on a song's steps, hit in time.\n- const rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right'] (the actions, one a lane),\n  windows: { perfect: 40, great: 80, good: 120 } (ms either side), life: .5, lead: 1.6 (seconds of notes shown\n  ahead), voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .2, dur: .09 } (the call notes' sound), on: { judge(j, note), fail(rh),\n  done(rh) } }).\n- chart: a string a lane, a character a step of the song: 'x' a note, 'h' a held note's head and '=' while it is\n  held, 'c' a call (PaRappa's teacher: it sounds and shows, the player answers after), '.' none; '|' and spaces are\n  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\n- rh.start() plays the song from its start, synced (it pauses with the game); rh.update() each step after the input:\n  a lane's press is judged by its distance in ms from its nearest note's time on the music clock (game.audio.pos:\n  game time, never the sound's own), a hold let go before its end drops, a note past the good window is missed, a\n  call sounds on its step (game.audio.sfx(voice, { step })).\n- rh.hit(lane), rh.release(lane): play a lane without its action (a bot, a lane of your own on a touch screen).\n- State: score, combo, maxCombo, counts { perfect, great, good, miss }, life (0..1, at 0 failed), accuracy (0..1),\n  grade ('S' 'A' 'B' 'C' 'D'), done, failed, last ({ j, lane, ms, t }: the last judgment, for its flash), notes\n  (each { lane, step, end, call, j, ms }), total (the notes to play).\n- rh.ahead() -> the notes to show: [{ note, dt (seconds to its time, < 0 past it), dtEnd }]; rh.draw(r, { x, y (the\n  target line's middle), dir: 'down' | 'up' | 'left' | 'right' (the way notes travel), len: 150 (pixels for lead\n  seconds), gap: 24 (between lanes), size: 8, colors, arrows: false (four lanes' notes as arrows: left, down, up,\n  right), call: false (draw the call notes instead) }) draws a highway on the overlay: the lanes, their targets, notes\n  and holds, each lane's flash.\n\n```js rhythm\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }); game.start({ update() {}, draw() {} });\nconst song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, loop: false, len: 32, tracks: [{ wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] };\nconst rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart: ['x...x...', '..x.....', '......h===', '.'] });\nrh.start(); const hits = [[0, 0], [2, 1], [4, 0], [6, 2]];\nfor (let i = 0; i < 400 && !rh.done; i++) {\n  game.advance(1 / 120); const s = game.audio.pos.step;\n  for (const h of hits) if (!h.done && s >= h[0]) { rh.hit(h[1]); h.done = true; }\n  if (s >= 9) rh.release(2); rh.update();\n}\nif (rh.counts.perfect !== 4 || rh.combo !== 4 || rh.grade !== 'S') throw new Error(JSON.stringify(rh.counts));\n```\nRules: judge on the music clock (rh does), never on the sound's; give the player the audio offset (Settings, Sound:\nits calibration) and keep the windows generous on a phone; draw notes from rh.ahead() each frame.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module RHYTHM: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (the full engine) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * RHYTHM  charts (lane strings, parts or a track's notes), judgments in ms of the music clock, combos, life, grades,\n * holds, calls (call and response), a note highway in any direction\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst SCORE = { perfect: 300, great: 200, good: 100 }, LIFE = { perfect: .03, great: .02, good: .005, miss: -.1 }, CALL = ['C5', 'E5', 'G5', 'C6', 'E6', 'G6'];\nconst clean = s => String(s).replace(/[|\\s]/g, '');\n// a part's lane strings laid at a step: notes { lane, step, end, call }\nfunction lanesOf(lanes, at, out) {\n  lanes.forEach((s, lane) => {\n    const c = clean(s);\n    for (let i = 0; i < c.length; i++) {\n      const ch = c[i];\n      if (ch === 'x' || ch === 'c') out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + i, call: ch === 'c' });\n      else if (ch === 'h') { let j = i; while (c[j + 1] === '=') j++; out.push({ lane, step: at + i, end: at + j, call: false }); i = j; }\n    }\n----\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ROAD v0.88.0: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nOutRun's, Pole Position's, Hang-On's and Road Rash's view: the road a run of short segments, each a band of grass, rumble\nand road drawn smaller with its distance, bending and rising, and what stands beside it scaled the same way.\n- const road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 (a segment's length, world units), width: 2000 (half the road), lanes: 3,\n  rumble: 3 (segments a stripe), draw: 240 (segments ahead), fov: 100, height: 1000 (the camera over the road), colors:\n  { road: [a, b], grass: [a, b], rumble: [a, b], lane, wall: [a, b], roof, portal }, fog: { color, density: 5 } | null, sky:\n  a Backdrop (full engine) | '#color', square: true (one focal length: a unit across is a unit up on a screen of any\n  shape; without it the picture stretches to the screen's, as the arcades' did) }).\n- Build it: road.add(n, { curve: -6..6 (+ bends right), hill: units up (- down) over the n segments, tunnel: true,\n  colors }) (curves eased in and out); road.place(z, offset, what, scale): scenery at distance z, offset across (-1\n  and 1: the road's edges; beyond: roadside); what: an E.sprite or E.anim (scale: world units a pixel, 8) or {\n  draw(g, sx, sy, scale), w: its width in units }. road.length: the lap (it loops).\n- Each frame: road.draw(r, { z (the camera's distance along), x (across, in half roads), h (its height over the road),\n  turn (the sky's offset: add curve * speed each step), cars: [{ z, x, w, draw(g, sx, sy, scale) }] }) as an overlay\n  over the frame (in a split screen, in r.viewport). A hill's crest hides what lies past it. The player's car, drawn\n  at the screen's bottom, is road.ahead(h) past z.\n- For the game: road.curveAt(z) (how hard it bends there: the push outward), road.yAt(z) (its height), road.hits(z, x,\n  w) (the scenery a body w half roads wide touches there), road.project(z, x, y) -> [sx, sy, scale] for the camera\n  last drawn (scale * a width in units = pixels).\n\n```js road\nconst E = My3D2dge, road = new E.Road({ segment: 200 });\nroad.add(50); road.add(60, { curve: 4, hill: 1200 }); road.add(40, { curve: -3, hill: -1200 }); road.place(3000, -1.4, { w: 300, draw() {} });\nif (road.length !== 150 * 200 || road.curveAt(80 * 200) <= 0 || !(road.yAt(110 * 200) > 0) || road.hits(3000, -1.3, .1).length !== 1) throw new Error('a road');\n```\nRules: z grows ahead and wraps at road.length; x is in half roads (0 the middle line); build the road before the first\ndraw; cars and scenery are drawn far to near after the road under them.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ROAD: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * ROAD  the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, scenery, tunnels\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { clamp } = E, easeIn = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * u * u, easeInOut = (a, b, u) => a + (b - a) * (-Math.cos(u * Math.PI) / 2 + .5);\nconst COLORS = { road: ['#6a6a6a', '#646464'], grass: ['#10aa10', '#009a00'], rumble: ['#e8e8e8', '#c01818'], lane: '#d8d8d8', wall: ['#5a4a3a', '#4a3a2a'], roof: '#2a2420', portal: '#6a5a48' };\nclass Road {\n  /** new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above) */\n  constructor(o = {}) {\n    /** o: its options (colors over the defaults) */\n    this.o = Object.assign({ segment: 200, width: 2000, lanes: 3, rumble: 3, draw: 240, fov: 100, height: 1000, fog: { color: '#a0c0e0', density: 5 }, sky: '#6aa8e8' }, o);\n----\n/*!\nmy-3D2dge module MODE7 v0.88.0: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everything on it scaled by its distance\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nSuper Mario Kart's, F-Zero's and Pilotwings' view (the SNES's Mode 7): a camera at a height over a flat floor, looking\nalong a heading, pitched down; the floor drawn a screen row at a time, the sky above the horizon, and on the floor\nbillboards (rigs drawn at the size their distance gives, sprites, your own drawing) far to near.\n- const m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: a TileMap (its floorTex) | (x, y) => [r, g, b] | a canvas (a texel a unit), size:\n  [w, h] (the floor in world units, for a function), outside: '#24402a' (beyond the floor) | wrap: true (it repeats),\n  sky: a Backdrop (full engine) | ['#top', '#bottom'], fog: { color, near, far } (far: nothing past it), far: 2400 }).\n- m7.cam = { x, y, h: 40 (height), angle: 0 (the heading, as E.angleTo gives it: 0 east, PI / 2 south; keep it\n  unwrapped, the sky turns with it), pitch: 12 (degrees down), fov: 70 (degrees across the height) };\n  m7.chase(body, { back: 56, h: 34, angle }) puts it behind a body (body.angle, or angle) each step.\n- In draw: m7.rig(rig, x, y, z), m7.sprite(spr or E.anim, x, y, z, { scale, flip, t }), m7.shape(id, x, y, z, { facing,\n  size, params, mats }) (full engine), m7.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => ...) gather billboards (k: screen pixels per world\n  unit there); m7.draw(r, cam) draws sky, floor, fog and them, far to near, as an overlay (in a split screen, in\n  r.viewport: give each player's cam). A billboard is flat, at its foot's scale: hit-test the box it was drawn in (from\n  m7.project and its size), not the world's view of it.\n- m7.project(x, y, z) -> [sx, sy, k] on the screen, or null behind the camera; m7.toFloor(sx, sy) -> [x, y], or null\n  above the horizon (both for the camera last drawn: HUD markers, a tap on the track). m7.horizon: its screen row.\n- Your own pass: m7.begin({ W, H, x, y, cx, cy, focal }, cam), then project, rowDepth(sy), drawFloor(g, rect),\n  view(k) (the engine view a rig is drawn with at k).\n- Resolution: the game's own pixels by default, as the SNES drew; m7.fullRes(game, true) each step draws at the\n  screen's own (sharper, slower; it returns the pixel size the game had), false gives the game's pixels back.\n\n```js mode7\nconst E = My3D2dge, m7 = new E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => ((x >> 4) + (y >> 4)) & 1 ? [80, 160, 80] : [60, 130, 60], size: [512, 512] });\nm7.cam = { x: 256, y: 400, h: 40, angle: -Math.PI / 2, pitch: 12, fov: 70 };\nm7.begin({ W: 320, H: 240 });\nconst p = m7.project(256, 300, 0), q = m7.toFloor(p[0], p[1]);\nif (Math.abs(q[0] - 256) > .01 || Math.abs(q[1] - 300) > .01 || p[1] <= m7.horizon) throw new Error('a floor point and back');\n```\nRules: m7.draw covers its viewport (draw nothing under it you need to see); move the camera in update, not draw; a\nbody's angle and the camera's heading are the same angle; billboards are gathered again every frame.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module MODE7: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * MODE 7  a perspective floor a row at a time, its sky, billboards scaled by distance\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst { clamp } = E;\n// cos and sin, exact at the quarter turns (a camera looking due north projects as the stress test always did)\nconst trig = a => { let c = Math.cos(a), s = Math.sin(a); if (Math.abs(c) < 1e-12) c = 0; if (Math.abs(s) < 1e-12) s = 0; return [c, s]; };\nclass Mode7 {\n  /** new E.Mode7({ floor, size, outside, wrap, sky, fog, far }): a Mode 7 view (the manual above) */","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c21bae92-846f-4b71-8d0d-098b4791d47c","uuid":"918ae681-f764-4668-b963-a9fc61929f08","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:28:09.170Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module RHYTHM v0.88.0: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a highway\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine only. Needs: no other module.\n\nPaRappa's, Beatmania's, Dance Dance Revolution's and Space Channel 5's play: notes on a song's steps, hit in time.\n- const rh = new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right'] (the actions, one a lane),\n  windows: { perfect: 40, great: 80, good: 120 } (ms either side), life: .5, lead: 1.6 (seconds of notes shown\n  ahead), voice: { wave: 'square', vol: .2, dur: .09 } (the call notes' sound), on: { judge(j, note), fail(rh),\n  done(rh) } }).\n- chart: a string a lane, a character a step of the song: 'x' a note, 'h' a held note's head and '=' while it is\n  held, 'c' a call (PaRappa's teacher: it sounds and shows, the player answers after), '.' none; '|' and spaces are\n  ignored. Or { parts: { A: [lanes], B: [lanes] }, order: 'A A B A' } (the parts one after another), or { track: 1,\n  lanes: 4 } (that track's notes, a lane by pitch, a note held three steps or more a hold).\n- rh.start() plays the song from its 