{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HQaxNtvCUL3QeTsEoTNYy6","type":"tool_result","content":"5:## Units and the height rules\n22:## Examples\n47:## Contents\n108:## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n119:## 1. Math\n195:## 2. Pixel primitives\n214:## 2b. Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n220:## 3. Views (projections)\n247:## 4. Screen\n269:## 5. Input\n357:## 6. Pixel fonts\n368:## 7. Lighting\n387:## 8. Particles\n407:## 9. Renderer\n457:## 10. Game\n572:## 10b. Standard features\n589:## 10c. Boot\n594:## 10d. Tweens and scripts\n611:## 10e. Paths\n621:## 10g. Weather\n625:## 10k. Save slots\n648:## 11. Humanoid rig\n721:## 12. Blob rig\n741:## 13. Tile map\n805:## 13b. Materials\n826:## 14. Flow field\n844:## 15. Texture helpers for floortex functions\n855:## 16. Platform map\n889:## 16b. Platformer\n930:## 17. Body\n950:## 17b. Actions\n972:## 17c. Mover\n1011:## 17d. Perception\n1028:## 18. Bullets\n1048:## 19. Spatial hash\n1058:## 20. Audio\n1091:## 21b. Backdrops\n1099:## 21c. Props\n1104:## 21e. Shapes\n1116:## 21. Ui\n1175:## 21d. Shell\n1204:## 22. Gpu lighting (webgpu)\n1225:## 23. Sessions\n1234:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, \n1269:## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an \n1314:## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engin\n1352:## Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a met\n1433:## Module gen: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed \n1444:## Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers\n1503:## Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everythin\n1526:## Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never p\n1555:## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a\n1587:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roads\n1604:## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates an\n1633:## Module rpg: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage\n1652:## Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engi\n1660:## Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/mod\n1689:## Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, r\n1735:## Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in\n## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.bus(name = 'sfx')`: a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument) to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute and the player's settings: 'sfx', 'music', 'voice' (its level is voiceVolume) or 'master'. Returns a GainNode, or null where there \n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. sto\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens:\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music:\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`, `game.audio.voiceVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice bus (bus('voice'))\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c21bae92-846f-4b71-8d0d-098b4791d47c","uuid":"eb34b037-573e-4cfe-a5d1-4e2eb65ff9a8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:28:23.038Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"5:## Units and the height rules\n22:## Examples\n47:## Contents\n108:## The engine object (E = My3D2dge)\n119:## 1. Math\n195:## 2. Pixel primitives\n214:## 2b. Sprite frames, turns and swaps\n220:## 3. Views (projections)\n247:## 4. Screen\n269:## 5. Input\n357:## 6. Pixel fonts\n368:## 7. Lighting\n387:## 8. Particles\n407:## 9. Renderer\n457:## 10. Game\n572:## 10b. Standard features\n589:## 10c. Boot\n594:## 10d. Tweens and scripts\n611:## 10e. Paths\n621:## 10g. Weather\n625:## 10k. Save slots\n648:## 11. Humanoid rig\n721:## 12. Blob rig\n741:## 13. Tile map\n805:## 13b. Materials\n826:## 14. Flow field\n844:## 15. Texture helpers for floortex functions\n855:## 16. Platform map\n889:## 16b. Platformer\n930:## 17. Body\n950:## 17b. Actions\n972:## 17c. Mover\n1011:## 17d. Perception\n1028:## 18. Bullets\n1048:## 19. Spatial hash\n1058:## 20. Audio\n1091:## 21b. Backdrops\n1099:## 21c. Props\n1104:## 21e. Shapes\n1116:## 21. Ui\n1175:## 21d. Shell\n1204:## 22. Gpu lighting (webgpu)\n1225:## 23. Sessions\n1234:## Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, \n1269:## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an \n1314:## Module drive: cars on the ground plane, a race round a track, the drivers who race it (engin\n1352:## Module fight: one-on-one fighting: fighters with frame data, guards, throws, specials, a met\n1433:## Module gen: generated maps: rooms and corridors, BSP, caves, mazes and scatter, from a seed \n1444:## Module grid: square and hex grids: paths, ranges, lines, fields of view, fog, groups, movers\n1503:## Module mode7: a perspective floor drawn a row at a time, a sky that turns with it, everythin\n1526:## Module physics: 2D rigid bodies: circles, boxes, polygons, segments; fast balls that never p\n1555:## Module rhythm: charts on a song's steps, judged on the music clock: combos, grades, holds, a\n1587:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roads\n1604:## Module rooms: a world of rooms joined at their edges, the map of what was explored, gates an\n1633:## Module rpg: items, inventories, equipment, shops, a party's stats and levels, status, damage\n1652:## Module songs: the songbook: the kits' best songs and more, and jingles, tagged by mood (engi\n1660:## Module story: dialogue as data, flags and values, a quest log and emote balloons (engine/mod\n1689:## Module strategy: real-time strategy and simulation: selection, orders, armies, production, r\n1735:## Module terrain: destructible ground in the side plane: carved and added, walked on, drawn in\n## 20. Audio\n\n- `E.note(n)`: note name -> frequency: E.note('A4') = 440, E.note('C#5'), E.note('Bb2'). Numbers pass through\n- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\n- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.bus(name = 'sfx')`: a bus for a sound of the game's own (Web Audio nodes it makes on audio.ctx: a babble voice, a loop, an instrument) to connect to, so it follows the volume, the mute and the player's settings: 'sfx', 'music', 'voice' (its level is voiceVolume) or 'master'. Returns a GainNode, or null where there \n- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to set (ms: settings.audioOffset) and done is true; taps go on refining it. sto\n- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\n- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h . k k h . s . h .' } ] } tokens:\n- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\n- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\n- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), playing }\n- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\n- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\n- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the music clock, scheduled with the music:\n- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\n- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\n- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\n- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\n- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\n- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\n- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\n- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`, `game.audio.voiceVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects, music and the voice bus (bus('voice'))\n- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\n- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\n- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\n- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\n\n## 21b. Backdrops","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HQaxNtvCUL3QeTsEoTNYy6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
