28423-eb32-41ac-9de8-673a33233c05","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:45:29.963Z","request_id":"req_011CgjAg872AiCYZQFBAKyVS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015fZrwCWmqQY8z3XwACXvyf":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211853__x57f432/work/_research; grep -n \"pointerenter\\|mouseenter\\|pointerover\\|mouseover\" engine/dist/handoff/my-3d2dge.js | cut -c1-220 | head; grep -n \"blend\\b\\|blend(\" mocap/mocap.js | head -4 | cut -c1-200; cd mocap && node tools/anim-set.mjs mesh2motion.js cmu.js CMU_111.js CMU_22.js --clips \"Pushup,Meditate,Jumping Jacks,Sleeping,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dizzy,Idle_Subtle,Greeting,CMU:Run_Loop,CMU:Walk_Loop,Stretch_Yawn,Get_Up_From_Back,Waiting_Loop,Hop_One_Foot_Loop,Wave_Hello,111_38_part1,111_38_part2,111_39_part1,111_39_part2,111_39_part3,111_41_part3,22_14\" --name FITCLIPS --out ../spike/cut/fitclips.js --credit \"Mesh2Motion (CC0), Quaternius (CC0), CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses)\" 2>&1 | tail -2; cd ../engine/dist/handoff; sed -n 625,647p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-200; sed -n 1236,1240p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-300; grep -n \"class Dialog\" my-3d2dge.js | head -2; sed -n 1116,1169p API-INDEX.md | grep -n \"new E.Dialog\\|new E.Menu\\|menu\\.\\(rowAt\\|cursor\\|items\\)\" | cut -c1-320 | head -12","description":"Check HTML hover focus, blend, final clip cut, saves and dialog API","timeout":60000}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015fZrwCWmqQY8z3XwACXvyf","type":"tool_result","content":"47:  lib.blend = (a, b, k, out = new Float32Array(P * 3)) => { for (let i = 0; i < P * 3; i++) out[i] = a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * k; out.src = (k < .5 ? a : b).src; return out; };\nwrote ../spike/cut/fitclips.js: 23 clips from MESH2MOTION and CMU and CMU_111 and CMU_22, 560 key poses, 173 KB\n## 10k. Save slots\n\n- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, plac\n- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot \n- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocke\n- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, \n- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n- `saves.game` †: its game\n- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, num\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n9029:class Dialog {\n3:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n33:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center'\n35:- `menu.rowAt(i)` †: entry i's box on the screen, [x, y, w, h] in screen pixels: where a click or tap picks it (a test's feed('down') and feed('up') there)\n46:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c21bae92-846f-4b71-8d0d-098b4791d47c","uuid":"197e4d92-da0a-4eaf-93c5-4273a813059e","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:45:30.235Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"47:  lib.blend = (a, b, k, out = new Float32Array(P * 3)) => { for (let i = 0; i < P * 3; i++) out[i] = a[i] + (b[i] - a[i]) * k; out.src = (k < .5 ? a : b).src; return out; };\nwrote ../spike/cut/fitclips.js: 23 clips from MESH2MOTION and CMU and CMU_111 and CMU_22, 560 key poses, 173 KB\n## 10k. Save slots\n\n- `new E.Saves(game, o) → saves` †: game.saves (made when first read): o is menu.saves ({ slots, version, migrate, write, read })\n- `saves.any` †: is there any save to load (a title's Continue)?\n- `saves.autosave(o)` †: save to the autosave (what write() gives)\n- `saves.copy(from, to)` †: copy a slot's save onto another (over what is there); false when the first is empty\n- `saves.erase(slot)` †: erase a slot\n- `saves.get(slot)` †: a slot's save as it is stored, checked: null when empty; { slot, damaged: true } when it can't be read; { newer: true } from a newer version of the game; else { slot, data, plac\n- `saves.latest()` †: the most recent save that loads, or null (a title's Continue loads it)\n- `saves.list()` †: every slot, the autosave first: [{ slot, empty, place, level, time, at, damaged, newer }] (a menu's rows)\n- `saves.load(slot)` †: load a slot: its data brought up to this version (migrate), played set from it, read(save) called. Returns the save ({ data, place, level, time, slot }), or null when the slot \n- `saves.save(slot, o)` †: save to a slot (0.., or 'auto'): o ({ data, place, level }) or what write() gives. Returns true when it is kept (in storage, or for the visit when storage is blocked: blocke\n- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, \n- `saves.blocked = false` †: storage refused a save (they last for the visit)\n- `saves.canSave = true` †: the pause menu offers Save (a JRPG turns it off away from save points)\n- `saves.game` †: its game\n- `saves.migrate` †: an older version's data brought up to this one (or null: kept as it is)\n- `saves.played = 0` †: seconds played in the game's scenes (paused time and titles left out), saved with each save and set by a load\n- `saves.read` †: what a load does with { data, place, level, time, slot }\n- `saves.slots` †: how many slots besides the autosave (3)\n- `saves.version` †: the game's version of its data (1), saved with each save\n- `saves.write` †: what a save holds ({ data, place, level })\n\n- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, num\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n9029:class Dialog {\n3:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, width, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it