{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjBj3URLPy1KU2ahUQsT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Kf4X2ZHjecCXyCFTbvYpyV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211853__x57f432/work && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='PLAN.md'; s=open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\ndef rep(a,b,count=1):\n    global s\n    assert a in s, a[:70]\n    s=s.replace(a,b,count)\n\n# section 2: the card also says what you can and can't do\nrep(\"Card (one sentence, device-correct controls, star targets, your best)\",\n    \"Card (one sentence on what you can and can't do here, device-correct controls, star targets, your best)\")\n\n# section 3: real numbers for the Body Check row\nrep(\"| Body Check | 14 | 7 | 4 | 3 | 1.1 | .20 | none | see test | | | |\",\n    \"| Body Check | 14 | 7 | 4 | 3 | 1.1 | .20 | none | 50% | 76% | 99% | 100% |\")\n\n# section 4: star rules that hold for the tested numbers\nrep(\"**Stars from `pct` (0..1):** 1★ .35, 2★ .65, 3★ .90 unless stated. Every activity must satisfy: passive input earns under 1★; the average bot earns at least 1★; the good bot earns at least 2★. **Each activity is one registry entry**\",\n    \"**Stars from `pct` (0..1):** 1★ .35, 2★ .65, 3★ .90 unless stated. Every activity must satisfy, on tier 1: passive input earns under 1★, the average bot at least 1★, the good bot at least 2★. On tier 2: passive under 1★, the good bot at least 1★, the expert bot at least 2★. **Each activity is one registry entry**\")\nrep(\"`pct` = .6 steadiness + .4 breath match (level within .25 of the guide). The instructor mirrors you on the next mat.\",\n    \"`pct` = .6 steadiness + .4 breath match (level within .25 of the guide), stars at .5, .75, .92 (doing nothing scores about .4 here). The instructor mirrors you on the next mat.\")\n\n# Step Class: four lanes, in the order the arrows expect (tested)\nrep(\"Tier 1: two lanes (left, right) at 100 bpm. Tier 2: four lanes (add up, down) at 120 bpm. 60 s, windows 45/90/135 ms.\",\n    \"Always four lanes in the order `arrows: true` draws: `lanes: ['stepL', 'stepD', 'stepU', 'stepR']`. Tier 1's charts use only left and right at 100 bpm; tier 2 uses all four at 120 bpm. 60 s, windows 45/90/135 ms, a song with `loop: false` and a `len`.\")\nrep(\"Charts are data, e.g. `{ parts: { A: ['x.......x.......', '....x.......x...'], B: ['x...x...x.......', '..x...x.....x...'] }, order: 'A A B A' }`.\",\n    \"Charts are data ✔: `{ parts: { A: ['x.......x.......', '.', '.', '....x.......x...'], B: ['x...x...x.......', '.', '.', '..x...x.....x...'] }, order: 'A A B A' }`.\")\n\n# section 8: no GPU lighting, performance is no goal\nrep(\"**Lights:** morning ambient about .92, noon lights off, dusk about .62 with warm lamps (`game.lights`). Keep bright scenes bright; a dark look is wrong here.\",\n    \"**Lights:** morning ambient about .92, noon lights off, dusk about .62 with warm lamps (`game.lights`). Keep bright scenes bright; a dark look is wrong here. Canvas lighting only: no `enableGPU`, and no WebGPU requirement for the hub.\\n\\n**Performance is not a goal.** Your brief treats the budget as unlimited, with frame rates and optimization out of scope: add the detail, crowd, particles and lights a scene wants, and don't spend time optimizing.\")\n\n# section 11: guard for Node, and the one engine change\nrep(\"\"\"document.addEventListener('pointerover', e => { const b = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.esh-sh button:not(:disabled), .esh-sh input:not(:disabled)');\n  if (b && e.pointerType === 'mouse') b.focus({ preventScroll: true }); });\"\"\",\n\"\"\"if (typeof document !== 'undefined') document.addEventListener('pointerover', e => {\n  const b = e.target.closest && e.target.closest('.esh-sh button:not(:disabled), .esh-sh input:not(:disabled)');\n  if (b && e.pointerType === 'mouse') b.focus({ preventScroll: true }); });\"\"\")\nrep(\"`E.Dialog` takes `{ bg: ['#ffffff', '#eaf6f8'], border: '#2cc6e6', color: '#20404c', nameColor: '#14a8c8' }`.\",\n    \"`E.Dialog` takes `{ bg: ['#ffffff', '#eaf6f8'], border: '#2cc6e6', color: '#20404c', nameColor: '#14a8c8' }`, but it hard-codes a near-black text shadow that smears on white. **Make this one engine change ✔:** in `class Dialog` in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, replace each `shadow: '#05040a'` used for the name, the text and the choices (3 places, around lines 9153 to 9176) with `shadow: this.shadow === undefined ? '#05040a' : this.shadow`, then set `talk.shadow = null`.\")\nrep(\"`menu.controls` names every action in plain words.\",\n    \"`menu.controls` names the actions in plain words and hides the ones a player has no reason to rebind.\")\n\n# section 14: Class needs a smaller map for half keyboards (tested)\nrep(\"(`game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`; `game.players[i]` has the same input API; keyboard players get `Input.halfKeys`).\",\n    \"(`game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`; `game.players[i]` has the same input API; keyboard players get `E.Input.halfKeys`). ✔ Half a keyboard runs out of keys with the full `INPUT` (the step and pace actions get none), so the Class scene sets its own `input`: the moves and menu actions plus `breath`, `catchL`, `catchR` only (left half F G H, right half `. / ,`), and its Step Class reads `lanes: ['left', 'down', 'up', 'right']`.\")\n\n# head: the hub reads \"Name — tagline\" from the title\nrep(\"<title>THE TITLE: a tagline</title>\", \"<title>THE TITLE — a tagline</title>\")\n\n# section 15: boot splash is markup, debug handle, external deps\nrep(\"writes head tags, boot splash (`E.bootSplash(title)`), CSS;\",\n    \"writes head tags, CSS, the boot markup at the start of `<body>` (copy the `e3-boot` div from `engine/game/index.html`);\")\nrep(\"Every activity becomes its own pausable scene, generated from the entry.\",\n    \"Every activity becomes its own pausable scene, generated from the entry. Set `game.debug = { snapshot() { return { scene, activity, tier, day, session, pct, stars, minutes, spineAge, lean, source }; } }`: tests and engine tools read it.\")\nrep(\"**Engine changes:** none are required. Everything here works through the public API plus the wrappers above. If you change `my-3d2dge.js`, note what and why for your Engine Feedback.\",\n    \"**Engine changes:** only the small Dialog shadow patch (section 11) is required. Everything else works through the public API and the wrappers above. Note whatever you change, and why, for your Engine Feedback.\")\nrep(\"7. Read `E.Input`'s labels with `input.label(a, device)` for both keyboard and mouse.\",\n    \"7. `E.Dialog` hard-codes a dark text shadow (section 11). The standard Settings list is long at 10 feet: rely on its scrolling focus and the zoom CSS.\")\n\n# section 16: file:// first, process manners\nrep(\"**`browser` (Playwright, one browser at a time, on the built file via `file://`):**\",\n    \"**`browser` (Playwright, one browser at a time, on the built file via `file://`, which needs no server):**\")\nrep(\"Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID.\",\n    \"Then open the game on its own and see it reach the title. Stop only your server, by its PID, never with `pkill`, `killall` or `fuser -k`.\")\n\n# finish line: research field\nrep(\"- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About screen, \\\"unknown\\\" for what you can't confirm, Usage as \\\"added on import\\\"\",\n    \"- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About screen, \\\"unknown\\\" for what you can't confirm, Usage as \\\"added on import\\\". Plan field: this plan's file name. Research field: what you actually did (further research is optional; this plan's recipes are already tested)\")\nopen(p,'w',encoding='utf-8').write(s)\nprint('ok', len(s))\nEOF\ngrep -n -i \"GameTitl