{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016zPuZHuvnPV6DP5qzb9VPv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Build plan: a wellness-retreat balance game inspired by Wii Fit\n2\t\n3\tYou are building this game alone, from this plan and your brief. Nobody can answer questions, so decide and move on.\n4\t\n5\t- **Your brief wins** on anything it states: deliverable names, the title rule, what the About screen lists, the exit interview. Where it leaves a choice, this plan has made it.\n6\t- **The title is yours.** Pick it the way your brief says. This plan says \"the title\" wherever it appears.\n7\t- **Paths here are relative to your dev folder.** The final file's name and place are in your brief.\n8\t- **✔ means tested.** It was run on this computer against engine v0.88.0 and hub client 1.4.0 while this plan was written. Trust those recipes. Numbers marked \"start\" are tuning defaults: change them with the dev sliders.\n9\t- Read sections 1 to 4 and 15 to 17 first. Use the rest as reference while you build each part.\n10\t\n11\t---\n12\t\n13\t## 1. The game\n14\t\n15\t**In one line:** a gentle, deadpan comedy about a five-day stay at a wellness retreat, where one analog skill, your balance, drives twelve short sports and exercise activities, coached by a needy talking scale and two serene wooden instructors.\n16\t\n17\t- **Genre:** sports and fitness minigame collection inside a light life-sim routine. Catalogue genre: Sports.\n18\t- **Perspective:** chosen per activity, always the clearest view of the body:\n19\t\n20\t| Where | View | Why |\n21\t|---|---|---|\n22\t| Studio activities | `brawler` (2.5D, fixed camera) | The whole body reads at 10 feet |\n23\t| The island | `threequarter`, follow camera | A small walkable place |\n24\t| Slalom | Mode 7, behind the skier | Speed |\n25\t| Jog | Pseudo-3D road, behind the runner | The coast rolling by |\n26\t| Tray | Custom steep view of the tray | You look down at what you tilt |\n27\t| Laundry Line | `side` | A rope is a line |\n28\t\n29\t**What to take from the source, in spirit:** a talking scale that judges you very politely; the morning weigh-in ritual and a number that matters too much; a clean, bright, faintly unsettling studio; calm instructors who never stop being pleasant; stillness treated as a sport; minutes banked and activities unlocked; little people jogging around an island.\n30\t\n31\t**What must stay original (this is a new game, not a recreation):** no Wii, Mii or Balance Board names, no copied characters, music, menus, minigame presentations or look. Say \"Wii Fit\" only in the Source Information your brief requires, and let the title riff on it as the brief says. Our cast, island, activities and jokes are below.\n32\t\n33\t**Never make fun of bodies.** There is no real weight, no BMI and no body-size talk. Tare weighs you in ducks. Jokes land on posture, wobbling, the player's excuses, and Tare's own loneliness.\n34\t\n35\t**Pillars. Cut anything that serves none of them.**\n36\t1. **One skill, many bodies.** Everything is the Lean (section 3). Learn it once, feel it everywhere.\n37\t2. **Your thumb is the body.** Squat depth *is* the stick. No canned animation that ignores your input.\n38\t3. **Polite, sincere, slightly hurt.** The game never winks and never sneers.\n39\t4. **The daily ritual.** Weigh-in, sessions, recap, bed. Tiny numbers feel huge.\n40\t5. **Ten-foot calm.** Bright, huge, one idea per screen.\n41\t\n42\t---\n43\t\n44\t## 2. What the player does\n45\t\n46\t```\n47\tTitle ──(10 s idle)──> Attract Mode loop ──(any input)──> Title\n48\t  ├ Continue / New Member ──> Member Card ──> Arrival (first time) ──> pick instructor\n49\t  │     Day loop: Bungalow ─> Body Check ─> Island ─> 3 Sessions ─> Evening recap ─> bed\n50\t  │     Day 5: The Gentle Games ─> Grand Stillness duel ─> Ending ─> Credits ─> Free Play\n51\t  ├ Class (2 to 4 players on one screen)\n52\t  ├ Free Play (after the ending, or from Dev Mode)\n53\t  ├ Settings   └ About / Credits\n54\tIn an AI Hub session: straight to the round, no title or menus (section 14).\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\t**A session (every activity, every time):** Card (one sentence on what you can and can't do here, device-correct controls, star targets, your best) → instructor demonstrates for 3 s with one line → \"Breathe in\" 3-2-1 → play for 45 to 90 s → stars stamp down, minutes drop into Gerald, Tare comments → Again / Done. Target: 2 to 3 minutes door to door. A story run takes 40 to 50 minutes and shows everything.\n58\t\n59\t---\n60\t\n61\t## 3. The core mechanic: the Lean\n62\t\n63\tEvery player has a **centre of balance** `p` (x right, y forward, both -1..1) with velocity `v`. Input sets a lean target `u`. The body chases it like a heavy person on an unstable board:\n64\t\n65\t```js\n66\t// one fixed step (dt = 1/120). nx, ny: smooth noise. fx, fy: scripted pushes (a gull, a gust, a thought)\n67\tax = k * (ux - px) - c * vx + s * px + A * nx(t) + fx;\n68\tay = k * (uy - py) - c * vy + s * py + A * ny(t) + fy;\n69\tvx += ax * dt; vy += ay * dt; px += vx * dt; py += vy * dt;\n70\tif (Math.hypot(px, py) >= 1) stumble();   // 1 s: input ignored, p eases home, stumble animation, score penalty\n71\t// noise: three sines with seeded phases\n72\tconst noise = (rng, f) => { const ph = [rng()*6.28, rng()*6.28, rng()*6.28];\n73\t  return t => (Math.sin(t*f+ph[0]) + .6*Math.sin(t*f*1.73+ph[1]) + .35*Math.sin(t*f*2.61+ph[2])) / 1.3; };\n74\t```\n75\t\n76\t`k` is responsiveness, `c` damping, `s` instability (the further you lean, the further you fall), `A` tremble, `nf` tremble speed, `R` the target ring's radius. **Steadiness** is the share of time inside the ring.\n77\t\n78\t**Tested defaults (✔ simulated over 45 s runs with modelled players):**\n79\t\n80\t| Set | k | c | s | A | nf | R | Push (speed, every s) | Passive | Poor | Average | Good |\n81\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n82\t| Body Check | 14 | 7 | 4 | 3 | 1.1 | .20 | none | 50% | 76% | 99% | 100% |\n83\t| Sun Flow | 12 | 6 | 6 | 3.2 | 1.3 | .28 | .5, 9 | 53% | 78% | 99% | 100% |\n84\t| Stork Stand 1 | 12 | 5 | 13 | 3 | 1.5 | .24 | .6, 7 | 20% (5 falls) | 30% | 68% | 95% |\n85\t| Stork Stand 2 | 11 | 4.5 | 15 | 3.6 | 1.7 | .22 | .7, 6 | 22% (15 falls) | 15% | 29% | 54% |\n86\t| Quiet Candle | 10 | 5 | 11 | 1.4 | .8 | .20 | .55, 5 | 14% (4 falls) | 59% | 95% | 100% |\n87\t| Laundry Line | 10 | 3.5 | 16 | 3.5 | 1.2 | .40 | .9, 5 | 35% (19 falls) | 31% | 39% | 79% |\n88\t\n89\t**Bots use this model** (tests, attract, Class fill-ins). It reacts to where `p` was `tau` seconds ago:\n90\t`target = -gain * pSeen - damp * vSeen + noise * smoothNoise(t)`; `u += (target - u) * min(1, dt * 16)`; clamp length to 1.\n91\t\n92\t| Bot | tau | gain | damp | noise |\n93\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n94\t| poor | .34 | 1.1 | .22 | .16 |\n95\t| average | .25 | 1.4 | .30 | .08 |\n96\t| good | .18 | 1.8 | .36 | .04 |\n97\t| expert | .14 | 2.2 | .42 | .02 |\n98\t\n99\t**Input (the same game on three devices, each native).** All of it fills one `intent` object, and activities read only `intent`, never a device. Bots and attract fill the same object.\n100\t\n101\t| | Controller | Keyboard | Mouse |\n102\t|---|---|---|---|\n103\t| Lean | Left stick: `u` = stick position | WASD or arrows: **nudge**. While held, `u` moves toward the direction at 1.6/s; released, it drifts home at .5/s. Tapping makes fine corrections | Pointer: `u` = pointer offset from screen centre / (`r.H` × .33). It stays where you leave it |\n104\t| Breath / Effort | L2 or R2, analog (`input.value`) | Space (level ramps over 4 s) | Left button (same ramp) |\n105\t| Left/right catch | L1 / R1 | Q / E | Left / right button |\n106\t| Confirm, Back, Pause | ✕, ○, Options | Enter or Space, Esc, Esc or P | Click, right click, the corner button |\n107\t\n108\t✔ Read the source like this. `input.lastDevice` becomes `'gamepad'` for a pad, but **moving the mouse does not change it away from `'keyboard'`**, so compare `input.mouse.t` (when the mouse last moved) with the time of your last key press. Use `input.pointer()` for the position. With a mouse, also hide the OS cursor over the canvas during activities and draw a small soft hand instead.\n109\t\n110\t✔ The input map must keep the engine's menu actions. **A custom map replaces the whole preset**: without `confirm` and `start`, menus and the hub card's Enter silently stop working.\n111\t\n112\t```js\n113\tconst D = E.Input.DEFAULT, INPUT = { up: D.up, down: D.down, left: D.left, right: D.right, start: D.start, pause: D.pause,\n114\t  confirm: D.confirm, cancel: D.cancel,\n115\t  breath: ['Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad6', 'Pad7'], catchL: ['KeyQ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad4'], catchR: ['KeyE', 'Mouse2', 'Pad5'],\n116\t  jump: ['Space', 'Pad0'], interact: ['KeyE', 'Enter', 'Pad0'], more: ['Tab', 'KeyM', 'Pad3'], retry: ['KeyR', 'Pad2'],\n117\t  paceL: ['KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad6'], paceR: ['KeyK', 'Mouse2', 'Pad7'],\n118\t  stepL: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Mouse0', 'Pad14', 'PadAxisLeft'], stepR: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Mouse2', 'Pad15', 'PadAxisRight'],\n119\t  stepU: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'WheelUp', 'Pad12', 'PadAxisUp'], stepD: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'WheelDown', 'Pad13', 'PadAxisDown'] };\n120\t```\n121\t\n122\t**The Plate** is the game's signature HUD: a large white disc at bottom centre (✔ radius 26 at `r.H - 34` reads well) with the ring, the dot, and a fading trail of the last second. In-ring: the ring glows mint, a soft chime rises with the streak, small glints appear. Near the edge: the rig flails, a creak plays, the controller rumbles harder (`input.rumble`). **Gentle Mode** (a setting): ring ×1.25, `s` and `A` ×.7. Tare says: \"Gentle Mode is on. I won't tell anyone. I don't know anyone.\"\n123\t\n124\t---\n125\t\n126\t## 4. The activities\n127\t\n128\t**Stars from `pct` (0..1):** 1★ .35, 2★ .65, 3★ .90 unless stated. Every activity must satisfy, on tier 1: passive input earns under 1★, the average bot at least 1★, the good bot at least 2★. On tier 2: passive under 1★, the good bot at least 1★, the expert bot at least 2★. **Each activity is one registry entry** (section 15) with its numbers in `game/data/`. Tier 2 opens after 2★ on tier 1 and from Day 4.\n129\t\n130\t### Stillness\n131\t\n132\t**Stork Stand** (`hold`). Stand on one leg on the deck. Hold the dot in the ring, which moves to a new spot every 12 s. A gull lands on your outstretched arm: a constant push to that side (`fx` = ±2.5) until it leaves with a little kick. 45 s. `pct` = steadiness - .05 × falls. The rig tilts with `p` (section 9). Tier 2, **Eyes Closed**: the Plate disappears and the screen dims. You balance by the rig's tilt, a stereo tone (pan = x, pitch = y) and rumble. This is the tutorial, guided on Day 1: \"Lean\" (move into the ring), \"Hold\", \"Recover\" (gull).\n133\t\n134\t**Sun Flow** (`hold` + breath). Five poses, two breaths each: Low Lunge → Down Dog → Triangle → Warrior → Stork. A guide ring swells for 4 s (breathe in: hold L2/R2, Space or left button) and shrinks for 4 s (let go). Analog players match the level; on digital the level ramps ±1 over 4 s. Crossfade poses with `lib.blend` over .6 s. 80 s. `pct` = .6 steadiness + .4 breath match (level within .25 of the guide), stars at .5, .75, .92 (doing nothing scores about .4 here). The instructor mirrors you on the next mat. Setting: Breath Hold or Toggle.\n135\t\n136\t**Quiet Candle** (`candle`). Sit cross-legged (`Meditate`). A candle burns in front of you. Its flame reacts to the **speed** of the dot: `|v|` over .55 drains flame .4/s, in-ring refills .12/s. Thought bubbles drift in with captions and push you slowly their way (`f` 3 to 5 for 2.5 s), so you must correct gently; any jerk hurts the flame. One relight (-15%), then it ends. 60 s. `pct` = .6 steadiness + .4 mean flame. If the input is perfectly untouched for the first 20 s, the thoughts drift you out and Tare says: \"Did you put the controller down? I can tell. This is not that kind of stillness.\" Tier 2 adds Dennis's blender and a goose.\n137\t\n138\t### Strength (all three are `rep`: one code path, three data rows)\n139\t\n140\t**The Rail.** A vertical rail beside the rig; a bead rides it at the instructor's tempo. Your lean **is** the body: `depth = clamp(-py, 0, 1)` scrubs the exercise as you move, so holding the stick halfway holds you halfway. `k` 16, `c` 8, `s` 0 on the main axis; the other axis has `s` 8 and is **form**: drift there and the rig visibly twists. Each rep scores 1.0 if mean `|depth - bead|` ≤ .08, 0 at ≥ .35, and shows Perfect/Good/Late. Tempo: 2 s down, 2 s up (tier 2: 3 s down, a hold, 1 s up). **Fatigue:** after 60% of the reps, `A` rises, `k` falls and the rig shakes. **\"Two more\":** if you are scoring above .8, the instructor adds two bonus reps. (\"You're doing so well, so I've added some.\") `pct` = mean rep × (1 - form penalty, up to .3).\n141\t\n142\t| Activity | Reps | Drive | Rig | Facing `tgt` |\n143\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n144\t| **Squat Rail** | 8 / 12 | down = deep | ✔ clip `22_14`: t = 1.1 (top) to 1.72 (bottom) | 1.2 |\n145\t| **Push-Up** | 6 / 10 | down = low | ✔ clip `Pushup`: t = 0 (top) to dur × .5 (bottom) | .1 |\n146\t| **Side Lunge** | 8 / 12 (horizontal rail; bead swings left and right) | `u = px` | ✔ `body` override `sideLunge(u)` (section 9) | π/2 |\n147\t\n148\t### Cardio\n149\t\n150\t**Step Class** (`step`, `E.Rhythm`). A bench, an instructor, three Regulars behind you all stepping on the beat. Always four lanes in the order `arrows: true` draws: `lanes: ['stepL', 'stepD', 'stepU', 'stepR']`. Tier 1's charts use only left and right at 100 bpm; tier 2 uses all four at 120 bpm. 60 s, windows 45/90/135 ms, a song with `loop: false` and a `len`. Input: d-pad or stick flicks, arrows or WASD, mouse buttons and wheel (see `INPUT`). The rig steps with `stepUp(k)`, triggered by your press, not by the chart. `pct` = `rh.accuracy`; stars at .5, .75, .92. Draw `rh.draw` with `arrows: true`, large, above the Plate's place. **Trap: music is 10% by default, so the beat must not depend on it.** Play a soft click on the sfx bus with `audio.onBeat`, and the instructor counts in gibberish on the beat. Charts are data ✔: `{ parts: { A: ['x.......x.......', '.', '.', '....x.......x...'], B: ['x...x...x.......', '.', '.', '..x...x.....x...'] }, order: 'A A B A' }`.\n151\t\n152\t**Hoop Hips** (`hoop`). Circle the lean to spin a hoop. Only movement with `|u|` > .55 counts; angular speed fills a big dial: \"Too slow / Just right / Too eager\". The good band is 7 to 11 rad/s (keyboard, by quadrant steps W→D→S→A: ×.6; mouse: circles round the screen centre, same as the stick). Regulars toss hoops from the sides: press catch left/right (L1/R1, Q/E, buttons) inside ±.25 s of arrival to stack it, up to 6. More hoops score faster and need a little more speed. 1.5 s out of band drops the top hoop. Halfway: \"Other way!\" 60 s. Mr. Okafor cheers. `pct` = score / best possible. ✔ Rig: `hula(phase)`. ✔ Hoops: back half queued with `bias: -6`, front half `bias: 6`.\n153\t\n154\t**Coastal Jog** (`jog`, `E.Road`; copy `engine/kits/road.js`). Alternate L2/R2 (J/K; left/right buttons) to set a cadence; lean steers. Stay in Marisol's pacing zone (cadence band 2.6 to 3.4 steps/s, shown as a calm gauge). Sprint over 4.2 for 2 s and you get a Stitch (3 s hobble). Weave round pigeons and other joggers, grab water cups. About 70 s for a lap. `pct` = .7 time in zone + .3 cups. Rig: `Run_Loop` scaled by cadence, drawn on the overlay from behind. Lou on his bench, the pier and bungalows go by as scenery.\n155\t\n156\t### Balance games\n157\t\n158\t**Mount Posture Slalom** (`slalom`, `E.Mode7`; copy `engine/kits/kart.js`). Lean left/right steers, forward tucks (speed ×1.35), back brakes (×.6). 18 gates (data: x offsets), base speed 220 units/s (start), about 60 s. A missed gate is +3 s; a snowman or pine is a 1.2 s tumble. `pct` from time between `par` and `worst`. Weather `snow`. Billboards: rig in `pose: 'crouch'`, skis, gates, snowmen. Show Regulars' times at the finish (\"Gertrude 0:58. She walked.\"). Tier 2: narrower gates and fog.\n159\t\n160\t**Tray Service** (`tray`, `E.Physics`, `sleep: false`). Dennis needs olives in cocktail glasses. He cannot say why. Lean tilts a tea tray: `world.gravity = [px * G, -py * G]` with G 420 (start), then `world.wake()`. Olives are circles; glasses are sensors (`on.enter` → plop, remove). Three trays in one run: 3 olives, then 5 with bumpers and a gap, then 7 with a slowly walking gecko. Layouts are ASCII in `game/data/trays.js`. 60 s total. `pct` = olives in / total × (.8 + .2 × time left share). Draw the tray with `new E.View('tray', 'Tray', 0, 55, 1, 1)` and tilt corners by `p` so the tilt is visible. Excellent with a mouse.\n161\t\n162\t**Laundry Line** (`laundry`, `side` view). Walk a clothesline between bungalows, x axis only, with the Laundry Line set. Walk speed is the Effort trigger (R2 analog; Space or left button .6); going faster adds up to +4 to `s`. Jump (✕, Space) over clothespins; in the air `p` freezes. Gusts (`fx` ±9 for .6 s) are telegraphed .8 s early by wind lines and a flying sock. Fall: you dangle, drop into a hamper, restart from the last post, -3 s. Three spans, about 70 s. `pct` from time, -.06 per fall. Sign: \"Please do not walk on the laundry line. Walking on the laundry line: 10:30 daily.\"\n163\t\n164\t### The Gentle Games (Day 5)\n165\tShort versions in order, one continuous festival with bunting, music and crowd: Stork Stand, Step Class, Slalom, then **the Grand Stillness**, a Quiet Candle duel with Gertrude on a raft at dusk (90 s). Two flames, hers and yours. Distractions escalate: gull, blender, conga line, fireworks (`game.flash` soft, respect Comfort), Tare singing, a goose. Her flame only weakens after 75 s, and only if yours is above half. Win or lose, the story continues; winning gives -1 Spine Age and her line: \"Well done, dear. I've been waiting since Thursday.\"\n166\t\n167\t---\n168\t\n169\t## 5. Progress\n170\t\n171\t**Spine Age** is the number that matters. Each discipline's score D (0..100) = mean over its activities of best stars × 33.3 (unplayed 0). O = mean of the four D. `SpineAge = round(78 - .58 × O)`, plus -1 for a Grand Stillness win. Start: 71. (\"Let's call it 71. It doesn't go higher. It's not allowed.\") Gertrude's is 19, Tare mentions it often. Show it as a big number, a one-line graph (one dot per day, never more than 8 dots) and a four-petal flower for the disciplines. Nothing denser.\n172\t\n173\t**Minutes and Gerald.** Gerald is a ceramic hippo with a coin slot who swallows your minutes. Earned: session minutes × (1 + .25 × stars), × 1.5 on Tare's Suggestion for the day. Coins fly up and clink in. Cumulative, never spent.\n174\t\n175\t| Minutes | Unlock (shows on the Bungalow rail and on your rig) |\n176\t|---|---|\n177\t| 5 | Towel |\n178\t| 10 | Headband |\n179\t| 15 | Sunhat |\n180\t| 20 | Tare wears a tiny bow tie |\n181\t| 25 | Gertrude's Spare Hat |\n182\t| 30 | Gerald gets a friend (a smaller hippo; no explanation) |\n183\t\n184\t**The five days:**\n185\t\n186\t| Day | Morning | Unlocks | Beats |\n187\t|---|---|---|---|\n188\t| 1 Orientation | Arrival card, pick instructor, first Body Check | Stork, Squat, Step, Tray | Forced guided Stork Stand counts as session 1 |\n189\t| 2 Improvement | Body Check | Sun Flow, Push-Up, Hoop, Laundry | Get 2★ today and Gertrude nods at you. That is the reward |\n190\t| 3 The Plateau | Body Check; Spine Age **held** at yesterday's | Candle, Lunge, Jog, Slalom | \"We call this the plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.\" |\n191\t| 4 Tare's Day | Spine Age catches up in one satisfying drop | Tier 2s | Tare's recalibration: a 30 s scene at Reception, Tare on a huge old scale, you press ✕ to read it. \"Three grams. It's the feelings. They're dense.\" |\n192\t| 5 The Gentle Games | Short Body Check | Everything | Games, duel, ending |\n193\t| After | Normal days, all open | | New daily Suggestion and Tips, forever |\n194\t\n195\t3 sessions a day. You may go to bed early (Tare says something). Tare's Suggestion marks one mat with a floating star.\n196\t\n197\t**Arrival:** \"You have been gifted a five-day stay at the Institute for Gentle Improvement. The card isn't signed. It only says: 'You know why.'\"\n198\t\n199\t**Ending reveal:** \"I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn't signed. That was me. I don't have hands. It took three years. I sent one to everybody. You're the one who came.\" ... \"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\" One extra line by final age: ≤24 Gertrude gives you the hat; 25 to 45 \"Your spine has stopped asking questions.\"; 46+ \"Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.\"\n200\t\n201\t**Body Check** (about 50 s): step onto Tare (hop, boop) → Stillness Test, 5 s, small ring → Lean Test, four directions, hold each 1 s → one Silly Question → Reading (\"Today you weigh 11.4 ducks. That is a normal number of ducks.\") → Spine Age, graph, remark, today's Suggestion. Questions (two pills, no effect beyond the remark): \"Have you recently sat?\" [Yes / Define recently]; \"Do stairs ever surprise you?\" [Often / Only the last one]; \"Do you make a small noise when you stand up?\" [Yes / No (this is a lie)]; \"On a scale of one to me, how do you feel?\" [One / Me]; \"When did you last look at your feet?\" [Just now / I'd rather not].\n202\t\n203\t**Members.** Three save slots shown as big Member Cards (rig portrait, nickname, Spine Age, Day). No text entry: avatar by pills (hair `short spiky long ponytail bald`, 6 skins, 8 tops, 4 bottoms) and a nickname from a list with Reroll (\"Gentle Doug\", \"Sir Slouch\", \"Ms. Almost\", \"The Other Pat\", ...). Use `game.saves` (`write`, `read`, `save(slot)`, `list()`, `latest()`). Autosave at dawn and after each session. Saves go through `saves.write`, so a test can reload them.\n204\t\n205\t---\n206\t\n207\t## 6. The island (hub)\n208\t\n209\tThe Institute for Gentle Improvement, on Lumbar Island. Motto on every sign: *Gently, Or Not At All.* A small `TileMap` in `threequarter`, about 44 × 26 cells. Crossing it takes 5 s. No enemies, no timer. Time passes only by doing sessions: morning light, noon, then dusk.\n210\t\n211\t```\n212\t~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n213\t~~^^^^^^~~~~~,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~~~~~~\n214\t~^^MT^^^^,,,,,,,,,,,,[STILLNESS DECK]=~~~~~~   ^ Mount Posture (snow; trailhead MT)\n215\t~~^^^^^,,,,,,,[RECEPTION],,,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~~~   , grass   . sand   = boardwalk   ~ sea\n216\t~~~,,,,,,,,,,,,,(Tare),,,,,,,,,,,[IRON ROOM]~\n217\t~~[BUNGALOW],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~~\n218\t~~,,(bed)(rail),,,[JUICE BAR],,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~\n219\t~~,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,(Dennis),,,,,[LAUNDRY POSTS]~\n220\t~~~,,,,,[BALANCE PARK],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~~\n221\t~~~~....(Tray)(Slalom sign).........=====~~~~   the pier: AEROBICS PIER\n222\t~~~~~~......................(Step)(Hoop)=~~~~\n223\t~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~(Jog start)~~~~~\n224\t```\n225\t\n226\t- **Mats** are glowing rugs: stand on one or click it to open the Card. Stillness Deck: Stork, Flow, Candle. Iron Room: Squat, Push-Up, Lunge. Pier: Step, Hoop, Jog. Park: Tray, Laundry posts, Slalom sign.\n227\t- **People:** the Regulars stand at set spots with a daily line and walk small loops. Tare hops behind you at a polite distance.\n228\t- **Bed** ends the day. **The rail** in the Bungalow is the wardrobe.\n229\t- **Controls:** stick or WASD walks; ✕ / E / Enter interacts; the mouse hovers (the person or mat highlights, a prompt shows) and clicks (walk there by `E.FlowField`, then interact). Clicking ground walks. Use `{ pick: thing }` on `r.actor`/`r.shape` and `r.pick(sx, sy)` for hover.\n230\t- **HUD:** top left Day and 3 session pips; top right Spine Age and Gerald's count, clear of `game.cornerArea()`. Nothing else.\n231\t\n232\t---\n233\t\n234\t## 7. Cast and voice\n235\t\n236\t**Tone rules.** Short sentences. Sincere, polite, a little too personal. Translated-instruction-manual cadence. No sarcasm, no meanness, no profanity, no pop-culture jokes, no references to being a game. Praise that wobbles. Facts nobody asked for. Tare is needy but never says so outright. Every text box: at most 2 lines of about 60 characters; a line is one thought. Use these lines verbatim and write as many more in the same voice as the game needs (aim for 150+ total, so a second playthrough still surprises). All text lives in `game/data/lines.js`.\n237\t\n238\t**Tare** (talking scale; \"tare\" is the button that zeroes one). A white slab with two soft footprints on top, a small dial, short legs, cyan LED eyes on the front edge and 8 faces (neutral, happy, worried, smug, shocked, sad, asleep, judging). Hops with squash and stretch. High, quick gibberish.\n239\t\n240\t- \"Oh! Feet. Good morning, feet.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c21bae92-846f-4b71-8d0d-098b4791d47c","uuid":"e107c8aa-b47a-4d07-9bcc-e7d3ab2b2765","timestamp":"2026-11-05T04:56:35.728Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan-v2__20261104-211853__x57f432/work/PLAN.md","content":"# Build plan: a wellness-retreat balance game inspired by Wii Fit\n\nYou are building this game alone, from this plan and your brief. Nobody can answer questions, so decide and move on.\n\n- **Your brief wins** on anything it states: deliverable names, the title rule, what the About screen lists, the exit interview. Where it leaves a choice, this plan has made it.\n- **The title is yours.** Pick it the way your brief says. This plan says \"the title\" wherever it appears.\n- **Paths here are relative to your dev folder.** The final file's name and place are in your brief.\n- **✔ means tested.** It was run on this computer against engine v0.88.0 and hub client 1.4.0 while this plan was written. Trust those recipes. Numbers marked \"start\" are tuning defaults: change them with the dev sliders.\n- Read sections 1 to 4 and 15 to 17 first. Use the rest as reference while you build each part.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The game\n\n**In one line:** a gentle, deadpan comedy about a five-day stay at a wellness retreat, where one analog skill, your balance, drives twelve short sports and exercise activities, coached by a needy talking scale and two serene wooden instructors.\n\n- **Genre:** sports and fitness minigame collection inside a light life-sim routine. Catalogue genre: Sports.\n- **Perspective:** chosen per activity, always the clearest view of the body:\n\n| Where | View | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Studio activities | `brawler` (2.5D, fixed camera) | The whole body reads at 10 feet |\n| The island | `threequarter`, follow camera | A small walkable place |\n| Slalom | Mode 7, behind the skier | Speed |\n| Jog | Pseudo-3D road, behind the runner | The coast rolling by |\n| Tray | Custom steep view of the tray | You look down at what you tilt |\n| Laundry Line | `side` | A rope is a line |\n\n**What to take from the source, in spirit:** a talking scale that judges you very politely; the morning weigh-in ritual and a number that matters too much; a clean, bright, faintly unsettling studio; calm instructors who never stop being pleasant; stillness treated as a sport; minutes banked and activities unlocked; little people jogging around an island.\n\n**What must stay original (this is a new game, not a recreation):** no Wii, Mii or Balance Board names, no copied characters, music, menus, minigame presentations or look. Say \"Wii Fit\" only in the Source Information your brief requires, and let the title riff on it as the brief says. Our cast, island, activities and jokes are below.\n\n**Never make fun of bodies.** There is no real weight, no BMI and no body-size talk. Tare weighs you in ducks. Jokes land on posture, wobbling, the player's excuses, and Tare's own loneliness.\n\n**Pillars. Cut anything that serves none of them.**\n1. **One skill, many bodies.** Everything is the Lean (section 3). Learn it once, feel it everywhere.\n2. **Your thumb is the body.** Squat depth *is* the stick. No canned animation that ignores your input.\n3. **Polite, sincere, slightly hurt.** The game never winks and never sneers.\n4. **The daily ritual.** Weigh-in, sessions, recap, bed. Tiny numbers feel huge.\n5. **Ten-foot calm.** Bright, huge, one idea per screen.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What the player does\n\n```\nTitle ──(10 s idle)──> Attract Mode loop ──(any input)──> Title\n  ├ Continue / New Member ──> Member Card ──> Arrival (first time) ──> pick instructor\n  │     Day loop: Bungalow ─> Body Check ─> Island ─> 3 Sessions ─> Evening recap ─> bed\n  │     Day 5: The Gentle Games ─> Grand Stillness duel ─> Ending ─> Credits ─> Free Play\n  ├ Class (2 to 4 players on one screen)\n  ├ Free Play (after the ending, or from Dev Mode)\n  ├ Settings   └ About / Credits\nIn an AI Hub session: straight to the round, no title or menus (section 14).\n```\n\n**A session (every activity, every time):** Card (one sentence on what you can and can't do here, device-correct controls, star targets, your best) → instructor demonstrates for 3 s with one line → \"Breathe in\" 3-2-1 → play for 45 to 90 s → stars stamp down, minutes drop into Gerald, Tare comments → Again / Done. Target: 2 to 3 minutes door to door. A story run takes 40 to 50 minutes and shows everything.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The core mechanic: the Lean\n\nEvery player has a **centre of balance** `p` (x right, y forward, both -1..1) with velocity `v`. Input sets a lean target `u`. The body chases it like a heavy person on an unstable board:\n\n```js\n// one fixed step (dt = 1/120). nx, ny: smooth noise. fx, fy: scripted pushes (a gull, a gust, a thought)\nax = k * (ux - px) - c * vx + s * px + A * nx(t) + fx;\nay = k * (uy - py) - c * vy + s * py + A * ny(t) + fy;\nvx += ax * dt; vy += ay * dt; px += vx * dt; py += vy * dt;\nif (Math.hypot(px, py) >= 1) stumble();   // 1 s: input ignored, p eases home, stumble animation, score penalty\n// noise: three sines with seeded phases\nconst noise = (rng, f) => { const ph = [rng()*6.28, rng()*6.28, rng()*6.28];\n  return t => (Math.sin(t*f+ph[0]) + .6*Math.sin(t*f*1.73+ph[1]) + .35*Math.sin(t*f*2.61+ph[2])) / 1.3; };\n```\n\n`k` is responsiveness, `c` damping, `s` instability (the further you lean, the further you fall), `A` tremble, `nf` tremble speed, `R` the target ring's radius. **Steadiness** is the share of time inside the ring.\n\n**Tested defaults (✔ simulated over 45 s runs with modelled players):**\n\n| Set | k | c | s | A | nf | R | Push (speed, every s) | Passive | Poor | Average | Good |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Body Check | 14 | 7 | 4 | 3 | 1.1 | .20 | none | 50% | 76% | 99% | 100% |\n| Sun Flow | 12 | 6 | 6 | 3.2 | 1.3 | .28 | .5, 9 | 53% | 78% | 99% | 100% |\n| Stork Stand 1 | 12 | 5 | 13 | 3 | 1.5 | .24 | .6, 7 | 20% (5 falls) | 30% | 68% | 95% |\n| Stork Stand 2 | 11 | 4.5 | 15 | 3.6 | 1.7 | .22 | .7, 6 | 22% (15 falls) | 15% | 29% | 54% |\n| Quiet Candle | 10 | 5 | 11 | 1.4 | .8 | .20 | .55, 5 | 14% (4 falls) | 59% | 95% | 100% |\n| Laundry Line | 10 | 3.5 | 16 | 3.5 | 1.2 | .40 | .9, 5 | 35% (19 falls) | 31% | 39% | 79% |\n\n**Bots use this model** (tests, attract, Class fill-ins). It reacts to where `p` was `tau` seconds ago:\n`target = -gain * pSeen - damp * vSeen + noise * smoothNoise(t)`; `u += (target - u) * min(1, dt * 16)`; clamp length to 1.\n\n| Bot | tau | gain | damp | noise |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| poor | .34 | 1.1 | .22 | .16 |\n| average | .25 | 1.4 | .30 | .08 |\n| good | .18 | 1.8 | .36 | .04 |\n| expert | .14 | 2.2 | .42 | .02 |\n\n**Input (the same game on three devices, each native).** All of it fills one `intent` object, and activities read only `intent`, never a device. Bots and attract fill the same object.\n\n| | Controller | Keyboard | Mouse |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Lean | Left stick: `u` = stick position | WASD or arrows: **nudge**. While held, `u` moves toward the direction at 1.6/s; released, it drifts home at .5/s. Tapping makes fine corrections | Pointer: `u` = pointer offset from screen centre / (`r.H` × .33). It stays where you leave it |\n| Breath / Effort | L2 or R2, analog (`input.value`) | Space (level ramps over 4 s) | Left button (same ramp) |\n| Left/right catch | L1 / R1 | Q / E | Left / right button |\n| Confirm, Back, Pause | ✕, ○, Options | Enter or Space, Esc, Esc or P | Click, right click, the corner button |\n\n✔ Read the source like this. `input.lastDevice` becomes `'gamepad'` for a pad, but **moving the mouse does not change it away from `'keyboard'`**, so compare `input.mouse.t` (when the mouse last moved) with the time of your last key press. Use `input.pointer()` for the position. With a mouse, also hide the OS cursor over the canvas during activities and draw a small soft hand instead.\n\n✔ The input map must keep the engine's menu actions. **A custom map replaces the whole preset**: without `confirm` and `start`, menus and the hub card's Enter silently stop working.\n\n```js\nconst D = E.Input.DEFAULT, INPUT = { up: D.up, down: D.down, left: D.left, right: D.right, start: D.start, pause: D.pause,\n  confirm: D.confirm, cancel: D.cancel,\n  breath: ['Space', 'Mouse0', 'Pad6', 'Pad7'], catchL: ['KeyQ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad4'], catchR: ['KeyE', 'Mouse2', 'Pad5'],\n  jump: ['Space', 'Pad0'], interact: ['KeyE', 'Enter', 'Pad0'], more: ['Tab', 'KeyM', 'Pad3'], retry: ['KeyR', 'Pad2'],\n  paceL: ['KeyJ', 'Mouse0', 'Pad6'], paceR: ['KeyK', 'Mouse2', 'Pad7'],\n  stepL: ['KeyA', 'ArrowLeft', 'Mouse0', 'Pad14', 'PadAxisLeft'], stepR: ['KeyD', 'ArrowRight', 'Mouse2', 'Pad15', 'PadAxisRight'],\n  stepU: ['KeyW', 'ArrowUp', 'WheelUp', 'Pad12', 'PadAxisUp'], stepD: ['KeyS', 'ArrowDown', 'WheelDown', 'Pad13', 'PadAxisDown'] };\n```\n\n**The Plate** is the game's signature HUD: a large white disc at bottom centre (✔ radius 26 at `r.H - 34` reads well) with the ring, the dot, and a fading trail of the last second. In-ring: the ring glows mint, a soft chime rises with the streak, small glints appear. Near the edge: the rig flails, a creak plays, the controller rumbles harder (`input.rumble`). **Gentle Mode** (a setting): ring ×1.25, `s` and `A` ×.7. Tare says: \"Gentle Mode is on. I won't tell anyone. I don't know anyone.\"\n\n---\n\n## 4. The activities\n\n**Stars from `pct` (0..1):** 1★ .35, 2★ .65, 3★ .90 unless stated. Every activity must satisfy, on tier 1: passive input earns under 1★, the average bot at least 1★, the good bot at least 2★. On tier 2: passive under 1★, the good bot at least 1★, the expert bot at least 2★. **Each activity is one registry entry** (section 15) with its numbers in `game/data/`. Tier 2 opens after 2★ on tier 1 and from Day 4.\n\n### Stillness\n\n**Stork Stand** (`hold`). Stand on one leg on the deck. Hold the dot in the ring, which moves to a new spot every 12 s. A gull lands on your outstretched arm: a constant push to that side (`fx` = ±2.5) until it leaves with a little kick. 45 s. `pct` = steadiness - .05 × falls. The rig tilts with `p` (section 9). Tier 2, **Eyes Closed**: the Plate disappears and the screen dims. You balance by the rig's tilt, a stereo tone (pan = x, pitch = y) and rumble. This is the tutorial, guided on Day 1: \"Lean\" (move into the ring), \"Hold\", \"Recover\" (gull).\n\n**Sun Flow** (`hold` + breath). Five poses, two breaths each: Low Lunge → Down Dog → Triangle → Warrior → Stork. A guide ring swells for 4 s (breathe in: hold L2/R2, Space or left button) and shrinks for 4 s (let go). Analog players match the level; on digital the level ramps ±1 over 4 s. Crossfade poses with `lib.blend` over .6 s. 80 s. `pct` = .6 steadiness + .4 breath match (level within .25 of the guide), stars at .5, .75, .92 (doing nothing scores about .4 here). The instructor mirrors you on the next mat. Setting: Breath Hold or Toggle.\n\n**Quiet Candle** (`candle`). Sit cross-legged (`Meditate`). A candle burns in front of you. Its flame reacts to the **speed** of the dot: `|v|` over .55 drains flame .4/s, in-ring refills .12/s. Thought bubbles drift in with captions and push you slowly their way (`f` 3 to 5 for 2.5 s), so you must correct gently; any jerk hurts the flame. One relight (-15%), then it ends. 60 s. `pct` = .6 steadiness + .4 mean flame. If the input is perfectly untouched for the first 20 s, the thoughts drift you out and Tare says: \"Did you put the controller down? I can tell. This is not that kind of stillness.\" Tier 2 adds Dennis's blender and a goose.\n\n### Strength (all three are `rep`: one code path, three data rows)\n\n**The Rail.** A vertical rail beside the rig; a bead rides it at the instructor's tempo. Your lean **is** the body: `depth = clamp(-py, 0, 1)` scrubs the exercise as you move, so holding the stick halfway holds you halfway. `k` 16, `c` 8, `s` 0 on the main axis; the other axis has `s` 8 and is **form**: drift there and the rig visibly twists. Each rep scores 1.0 if mean `|depth - bead|` ≤ .08, 0 at ≥ .35, and shows Perfect/Good/Late. Tempo: 2 s down, 2 s up (tier 2: 3 s down, a hold, 1 s up). **Fatigue:** after 60% of the reps, `A` rises, `k` falls and the rig shakes. **\"Two more\":** if you are scoring above .8, the instructor adds two bonus reps. (\"You're doing so well, so I've added some.\") `pct` = mean rep × (1 - form penalty, up to .3).\n\n| Activity | Reps | Drive | Rig | Facing `tgt` |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Squat Rail** | 8 / 12 | down = deep | ✔ clip `22_14`: t = 1.1 (top) to 1.72 (bottom) | 1.2 |\n| **Push-Up** | 6 / 10 | down = low | ✔ clip `Pushup`: t = 0 (top) to dur × .5 (bottom) | .1 |\n| **Side Lunge** | 8 / 12 (horizontal rail; bead swings left and right) | `u = px` | ✔ `body` override `sideLunge(u)` (section 9) | π/2 |\n\n### Cardio\n\n**Step Class** (`step`, `E.Rhythm`). A bench, an instructor, three Regulars behind you all stepping on the beat. Always four lanes in the order `arrows: true` draws: `lanes: ['stepL', 'stepD', 'stepU', 'stepR']`. Tier 1's charts use only left and right at 100 bpm; tier 2 uses all four at 120 bpm. 60 s, windows 45/90/135 ms, a song with `loop: false` and a `len`. Input: d-pad or stick flicks, arrows or WASD, mouse buttons and wheel (see `INPUT`). The rig steps with `stepUp(k)`, triggered by your press, not by the chart. `pct` = `rh.accuracy`; stars at .5, .75, .92. Draw `rh.draw` with `arrows: true`, large, above the Plate's place. **Trap: music is 10% by default, so the beat must not depend on it.** Play a soft click on the sfx bus with `audio.onBeat`, and the instructor counts in gibberish on the beat. Charts are data ✔: `{ parts: { A: ['x.......x.......', '.', '.', '....x.......x...'], B: ['x...x...x.......', '.', '.', '..x...x.....x...'] }, order: 'A A B A' }`.\n\n**Hoop Hips** (`hoop`). Circle the lean to spin a hoop. Only movement with `|u|` > .55 counts; angular speed fills a big dial: \"Too slow / Just right / Too eager\". The good band is 7 to 11 rad/s (keyboard, by quadrant steps W→D→S→A: ×.6; mouse: circles round the screen centre, same as the stick). Regulars toss hoops from the sides: press catch left/right (L1/R1, Q/E, buttons) inside ±.25 s of arrival to stack it, up to 6. More hoops score faster and need a little more speed. 1.5 s out of band drops the top hoop. Halfway: \"Other way!\" 60 s. Mr. Okafor cheers. `pct` = score / best possible. ✔ Rig: `hula(phase)`. ✔ Hoops: back half queued with `bias: -6`, front half `bias: 6`.\n\n**Coastal Jog** (`jog`, `E.Road`; copy `engine/kits/road.js`). Alternate L2/R2 (J/K; left/right buttons) to set a cadence; lean steers. Stay in Marisol's pacing zone (cadence band 2.6 to 3.4 steps/s, shown as a calm gauge). Sprint over 4.2 for 2 s and you get a Stitch (3 s hobble). Weave round pigeons and other joggers, grab water cups. About 70 s for a lap. `pct` = .7 time in zone + .3 cups. Rig: `Run_Loop` scaled by cadence, drawn on the overlay from behind. Lou on his bench, the pier and bungalows go by as scenery.\n\n### Balance games\n\n**Mount Posture Slalom** (`slalom`, `E.Mode7`; copy `engine/kits/kart.js`). Lean left/right steers, forward tucks (speed ×1.35), back brakes (×.6). 18 gates (data: x offsets), base speed 220 units/s (start), about 60 s. A missed gate is +3 s; a snowman or pine is a 1.2 s tumble. `pct` from time between `par` and `worst`. Weather `snow`. Billboards: rig in `pose: 'crouch'`, skis, gates, snowmen. Show Regulars' times at the finish (\"Gertrude 0:58. She walked.\"). Tier 2: narrower gates and fog.\n\n**Tray Service** (`tray`, `E.Physics`, `sleep: false`). Dennis needs olives in cocktail glasses. He cannot say why. Lean tilts a tea tray: `world.gravity = [px * G, -py * G]` with G 420 (start), then `world.wake()`. Olives are circles; glasses are sensors (`on.enter` → plop, remove). Three trays in one run: 3 olives, then 5 with bumpers and a gap, then 7 with a slowly walking gecko. Layouts are ASCII in `game/data/trays.js`. 60 s total. `pct` = olives in / total × (.8 + .2 × time left share). Draw the tray with `new E.View('tray', 'Tray', 0, 55, 1, 1)` and tilt corners by `p` so the tilt is visible. Excellent with a mouse.\n\n**Laundry Line** (`laundry`, `side` view). Walk a clothesline between bungalows, x axis only, with the Laundry Line set. Walk speed is the Effort trigger (R2 analog; Space or left button .6); going faster adds up to +4 to `s`. Jump (✕, Space) over clothespins; in the air `p` freezes. Gusts (`fx` ±9 for .6 s) are telegraphed .8 s early by wind lines and a flying sock. Fall: you dangle, drop into a hamper, restart from the last post, -3 s. Three spans, about 70 s. `pct` from time, -.06 per fall. Sign: \"Please do not walk on the laundry line. Walking on the laundry line: 10:30 daily.\"\n\n### The Gentle Games (Day 5)\nShort versions in order, one continuous festival with bunting, music and crowd: Stork Stand, Step Class, Slalom, then **the Grand Stillness**, a Quiet Candle duel with Gertrude on a raft at dusk (90 s). Two flames, hers and yours. Distractions escalate: gull, blender, conga line, fireworks (`game.flash` soft, respect Comfort), Tare singing, a goose. Her flame only weakens after 75 s, and only if yours is above half. Win or lose, the story continues; winning gives -1 Spine Age and her line: \"Well done, dear. I've been waiting since Thursday.\"\n\n---\n\n## 5. Progress\n\n**Spine Age** is the number that matters. Each discipline's score D (0..100) = mean over its activities of best stars × 33.3 (unplayed 0). O = mean of the four D. `SpineAge = round(78 - .58 × O)`, plus -1 for a Grand Stillness win. Start: 71. (\"Let's call it 71. It doesn't go higher. It's not allowed.\") Gertrude's is 19, Tare mentions it often. Show it as a big number, a one-line graph (one dot per day, never more than 8 dots) and a four-petal flower for the disciplines. Nothing denser.\n\n**Minutes and Gerald.** Gerald is a ceramic hippo with a coin slot who swallows your minutes. Earned: session minutes × (1 + .25 × stars), × 1.5 on Tare's Suggestion for the day. Coins fly up and clink in. Cumulative, never spent.\n\n| Minutes | Unlock (shows on the Bungalow rail and on your rig) |\n|---|---|\n| 5 | Towel |\n| 10 | Headband |\n| 15 | Sunhat |\n| 20 | Tare wears a tiny bow tie |\n| 25 | Gertrude's Spare Hat |\n| 30 | Gerald gets a friend (a smaller hippo; no explanation) |\n\n**The five days:**\n\n| Day | Morning | Unlocks | Beats |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 Orientation | Arrival card, pick instructor, first Body Check | Stork, Squat, Step, Tray | Forced guided Stork Stand counts as session 1 |\n| 2 Improvement | Body Check | Sun Flow, Push-Up, Hoop, Laundry | Get 2★ today and Gertrude nods at you. That is the reward |\n| 3 The Plateau | Body Check; Spine Age **held** at yesterday's | Candle, Lunge, Jog, Slalom | \"We call this the plateau. It is on the map. You cannot go around it.\" |\n| 4 Tare's Day | Spine Age catches up in one satisfying drop | Tier 2s | Tare's recalibration: a 30 s scene at Reception, Tare on a huge old scale, you press ✕ to read it. \"Three grams. It's the feelings. They're dense.\" |\n| 5 The Gentle Games | Short Body Check | Everything | Games, duel, ending |\n| After | Normal days, all open | | New daily Suggestion and Tips, forever |\n\n3 sessions a day. You may go to bed early (Tare says something). Tare's Suggestion marks one mat with a floating star.\n\n**Arrival:** \"You have been gifted a five-day stay at the Institute for Gentle Improvement. The card isn't signed. It only says: 'You know why.'\"\n\n**Ending reveal:** \"I should tell you something. The card. The one that wasn't signed. That was me. I don't have hands. It took three years. I sent one to everybody. You're the one who came.\" ... \"Now step off. Go on. I'll be here. I'm a scale. That's the whole job.\" One extra line by final age: ≤24 Gertrude gives you the hat; 25 to 45 \"Your spine has stopped asking questions.\"; 46+ \"Come back. Please. I mean that in a wellness way.\"\n\n**Body Check** (about 50 s): step onto Tare (hop, boop) → Stillness Test, 5 s, small ring → Lean Test, four directions, hold each 1 s → one Silly Question → Reading (\"Today you weigh 11.4 ducks. That is a normal number of ducks.\") → Spine Age, graph, remark, today's Suggestion. Questions (two pills, no effect beyond the remark): \"Have you recently sat?\" [Yes / Define recently]; \"Do stairs ever surprise you?\" [Often / Only the last one]; \"Do you make a small noise when you stand up?\" [Yes / No (this is a lie)]; \"On a scale of one to me, how do you feel?\" [One / Me]; \"When did you last look at your feet?\" [Just now / I'd rather not].\n\n**Members.** Three save slots shown as big Member Cards (rig portrait, nickname, Spine Age, Day). No text entry: avatar by pills (hair `short spiky long ponytail bald`, 6 skins, 8 tops, 4 bottoms) and a nickname from a list with Reroll (\"Gentle Doug\", \"Sir Slouch\", \"Ms. Almost\", \"The Other Pat\", ...). Use `game.saves` (`write`, `read`, `save(slot)`, `list()`, `latest()`). Autosave at dawn and after each session. Saves go through `saves.write`, so a test can reload them.\n\n---\n\n## 6. The island (hub)\n\nThe Institute for Gentle Improvement, on Lumbar Island. Motto on every sign: *Gently, Or Not At All.* A small `TileMap` in `threequarter`, about 44 × 26 cells. Crossing it takes 5 s. No enemies, no timer. Time passes only by doing sessions: morning light, noon, then dusk.\n\n```\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~^^^^^^~~~~~,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~~~~~~\n~^^MT^^^^,,,,,,,,,,,,[STILLNESS DECK]=~~~~~~   ^ Mount Posture (snow; trailhead MT)\n~~^^^^^,,,,,,,[RECEPTION],,,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~~~   , grass   . sand   = boardwalk   ~ sea\n~~~,,,,,,,,,,,,,(Tare),,,,,,,,,,,[IRON ROOM]~\n~~[BUNGALOW],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~~\n~~,,(bed)(rail),,,[JUICE BAR],,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~\n~~,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,(Dennis),,,,,[LAUNDRY POSTS]~\n~~~,,,,,[BALANCE PARK],,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,~~~~\n~~~~....(Tray)(Slalom sign).........=====~~~~   the pier: AEROBICS PIER\n~~~~~~......................(Step)(Hoop)=~~~~\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~(Jog start)~~~~~\n```\n\n- **Mats** are glowing rugs: stand on one or click it to open the Card. Stillness Deck: Stork, Flow, Candle. Iron Room: Squat, Push-Up, Lunge. Pier: Step, Hoop, Jog. Park: Tray, Laundry posts, Slalom sign.\n- **People:** the Regulars stand at set spots with a daily line and walk small loops. Tare hops behind you at a polite distance.\n- **Bed** ends the day. **The rail** in the Bungalow is the wardrobe.\n- **Controls:** stick or WASD walks; ✕ / E / Enter interacts; the mouse hovers (the person or mat highlights, a prompt shows) and clicks (walk there by `E.FlowField`, then interact). Clicking ground walks. Use `{ pick: thing }` on `r.actor`/`r.shape` and `r.pick(sx, sy)` for hover.\n- **HUD:** top left Day and 3 session pips; top right Spine Age and Gerald's count, clear of `game.cornerArea()`. Nothing else.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Cast and voice\n\n**Tone rules.** Short sentences. Sincere, polite, a little too personal. Translated-instruction-manual cadence. No sarcasm, no meanness, no profanity, no pop-culture jokes, no references to being a game. Praise that wobbles. Facts nobody asked for. Tare is needy but never says so outright. Every text box: at most 2 lines of about 60 characters; a line is one thought. Use these lines verbatim and write as many more in the same voice as the game needs (aim for 150+ total, so a second playthrough still surprises). All text lives in `game/data/lines.js`.\n\n**Tare** (talking scale; \"tare\" is the button that zeroes one). A white slab with two soft footprints on top, a small dial, short legs, cyan LED eyes on the front edge and 8 faces (neutral, happy, worried, smug, shocked, sad, asleep, judging). Hops with squash and stretch. High, quick gibberish.\n\n- \"Oh! Feet. Good morning, feet.\"","numLines":240,"startLine":1,"totalLines":656}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016zPuZHuvnPV6DP5qzb9VPv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
